{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019wsJSzp1HUeoBbyZjkzJvj","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Paper Framing — importance_margin_vla_compress\n2\t\n3\t## Target Venue\n4\t- Primary: **CoRL 2026** (Austin, Nov 9-12; abstract May 26, paper May 29)\n5\t- Timeline: 6 days to abstract, 9 days to paper (as of 2026-05-20)\n6\t\n7\t## Title (working)\n8\t\"Why Token Pruning Crashes Some Robot Policies but Not Others: The Role of Vision Connectors in VLA Token Compressibility\"\n9\t\n10\t## Core Insight\n11\tVLA token compressibility is determined by the vision connector architecture. Evidence from **5 VLA models spanning 3 connector families** reveals a clean taxonomy:\n12\t- **Linear projection** (π0 3.3B): pruning-immune offline. π0 k=0.1 normalized loss = 0.976 (improves 2.4%). Tokens independently projected, information uniform.\n13\t- **Linear projection + deep post-processing** (X-VLA 880M, linear proj + 12-layer BART encoder): robust k≥0.9 (97.6% SR), **cliff at k=0.7 (56.2% SR, -43pp)**. BART encoder introduces non-linear mixing that creates partial token dependencies. CV=0.151 (between π0=0.038 and OpenVLA=0.215).\n14\t- **Multi-layer MLP** (OpenVLA 7B, OpenVLA-OFT 7B): graded degradation. k=0.1 normalized loss = 1.608 (+61%). Non-linear mixing creates partial dependencies. OFT entropy (0.667) ≈ Standard (0.661), confirming connector — not action head — determines attention structure.\n15\t- **Pixel-shuffle** (SmolVLA 450M): catastrophic cliff-edge. k=0.95 (removing 5%) → 0% SR. Spatial folding creates irreversible entanglement.\n16\t\n17\tKey controlled comparison: π0 (256 tokens, linear) vs OpenVLA (256 tokens, 3-layer MLP) — same token count, same encoder lineage, only connector differs. k=0.1: π0 improves 2.4% vs OpenVLA degrades 61%. This isolates connector as the causal factor.\n18\t\n19\tLearned re-encoding (VTR) overcomes the cliff-edge: cross-attention 60.1±1.3% and MLP adapter 63.4±2.6% at M=32 (vs 0% hard pruning), with M=128 passthrough (58.0%±3.5, 3-seed) confirming the gain comes from re-encoding itself, not compression. SmolVLA M-curve confirmed flat (D105): M=16 (56.9%±1.3) = M=128 (58.0%±3.5), all 5 M-values within ±5pp. VTR achieves near-lossless compression at any ratio for pixel-shuffle connectors.\n20\t\n21\t## Paper Identity (Round 4 Upgrade, 2026-05-20)\n22\t**ANALYSIS + METHOD paper.** (D091 → D097: expanded from 2-3 models to 5 models across 3 connector families)\n23\t\n24\t**Analysis contribution (primary)**: First systematic study of why token pruning catastrophically fails on some VLA architectures. We show that the effective vision-to-LLM projection pipeline determines pruning robustness along a continuous spectrum (CV: 0.038→0.314): pure linear projection is immune, linear+deep post-processing shows a cliff pattern, MLP projectors degrade smoothly, and pixel-shuffle collapses catastrophically. 5 models across 4 model sizes (450M-7B) eliminate size confound. No competing work does cross-architecture VLA token analysis.\n25\t\n26\t**Method contribution**: Diagnose-then-Compress framework:\n27\t- Step 1: **Connector Compressibility Diagnostic** (D104: resolved)\n28\t  - **Primary metric: Importance CV** (token importance heterogeneity) — zero-cost, one forward pass\n29\t  - CV forms continuous spectrum predicting pruning tolerance: π0=0.038 < X-VLA=0.151 < OpenVLA=0.215 < SmolVLA=0.314\n30\t  - ⚠️ D106+: X-VLA CV=0.151 correctly predicted its intermediate pruning behavior (k=0.7 ≈50% SR ≈ OpenVLA k=0.7). CV is a valid continuous predictor, NOT a 3-class discrete classifier.\n31\t  - **Key discovery**: X-VLA \"linear projection\" passes through BART encoder (12 transformer layers) before decoder → introduces non-linear mixing → explains CV=0.151 (much higher than π0=0.038 pure linear)\n32\t  - **Entropy as mechanistic supplement**:\n33\t    - π0: entropy=0.959 (per-layer mean, range 0.931–0.983), CV=0.038 — uniform & independent → most tolerant\n34\t    - X-VLA: entropy=0.614, CV=0.151 — selective & BART-mixed → intermediate\n35\t    - OpenVLA: entropy=0.661, CV=0.215 — selective & MLP-mixed → graded\n36\t    - SmolVLA: entropy=0.952, CV=0.314 — near-uniform but spatially entangled → catastrophic\n37\t  - NOTE: X-VLA entropy=0.614 (NOT \"high\"), similar to OpenVLA 0.661. Both go through non-linear mixing.\n38\t  - ✅ Batch 2 complete: continuous CV spectrum confirmed (X-VLA full 8-point curve validates threshold-graded class)\n39\t  - Supplementary: lightweight pruning probe (remove 5%, one forward pass) as practitioner-friendly alternative\n40\t- Step 2: VTR (Vision Token Re-encoding) — lightweight cross-attention module (~22M params) for universal compression\n41\t- For entangled tokens (pixel-shuffle): recovers from 0% to 60%+, M-curve confirmed flat D105 (near-lossless at any compression ratio)\n42\t- For independent tokens (MLP projector): **D109 C4-ext confirmed 0% SR** at 20K steps (M=128, severe overfitting — model outputs identical action every step). VTR on MLP projector does NOT improve SR; reframed as \"VTR ceiling depends on connector type\" finding. User directive: performance degradation acceptable if efficiency improves — VTR value is 75% KV-cache reduction + attention speedup. VTC-only M=32/M=64 training in progress to test whether smaller M values fare better.\n43\t\n44\t**Differentiation from concurrent work**: 4 concurrent works (Compressor-VLA, SpecPrune-VLA, LightVLA ICRA'26, See What Matters ICML'26) all propose pruning on MLP-projector VLAs. We (1) explain why pruning fails on pixel-shuffle architectures, (2) identify why pruning succeeds on linear projection (tokens are truly independent), and (3) propose a re-encoding method motivated by the diagnostic analysis.\n45\t\n46\t**Model coverage**: 5 VLA models × 3 connector families × 4 model sizes (450M-7B). RC1 (only 2 models) and RC2 (size confound) fully addressed.\n47\t\n48\t## Core Claims (5 claims, expanded from 4)\n49\t\n50\t### Claim 1: Architecture-Dependent Compressibility (taxonomy — D107 RESOLVED)\n51\tThe effective vision-to-LLM projection pipeline determines pruning robustness. Evidence from 5 VLA models:\n52\t- **Pure linear projection** (π0): immune — k=0.1 loss improves 2.4%\n53\t- **Linear + deep post-processing** (X-VLA, BART 12L): **threshold-graded** — immune k≥0.9 (97.6%), threshold at k=0.7 (56.2%, -43pp), then graded degradation k≤0.5 (42.6%→23.0%→~4%→~0%). Distinct from SmolVLA's catastrophic cliff (any pruning → 0%)\n54\t- **Multi-layer MLP** (OpenVLA, OFT): smooth graded degradation. k=0.5 → 37.4% (-49% relative)\n55\t- **Pixel-shuffle** (SmolVLA): **catastrophic cliff** — k=0.95 (5% removal) → 0% SR. Any pruning destroys.\n56\t- **CV predicts degradation onset**: 0.038 (immune) → 0.151 (threshold-graded at k=0.7) → 0.215 (immediate onset) → 0.314 (catastrophic cliff)\n57\t\n58\t**Evidence**: 5 models, 3 connector families, 4 model sizes (450M-7B). Key controlled comparison: π0 (256 tokens, linear) k=0.1 = 0.976 vs OpenVLA (256 tokens, 3-layer MLP) k=0.1 = 1.608. Same token count, same encoder lineage, only connector differs. X-VLA cliff pattern (k=0.9: 97.6% → k=0.7: 56.2%) confirms intermediate CV predicts intermediate behavior.\n59\t\n60\t⚠️ **D108: Pruning method discrepancy** — Offline diagnostic uses L2_norm_zero_out (all models). But LIBERO closed-loop evals differ: OpenVLA = random removal (torch.randperm, physical), X-VLA = L2 norm removal (importance-based, physical). SmolVLA = all methods tested (all 0%). This STRENGTHENS findings (OpenVLA survives even random = hardest test; X-VLA cliffs even with importance-based = easiest test), but paper must accurately report. OpenVLA L2 norm comparison experiment planned for fair cross-model comparison.\n61\t\n62\t### Claim 2: Pixel Shuffle Creates Irreversible Token Entanglement\n63\tSmolVLA's pixel_shuffle connector spatially folds 1024 SigLIP patches into 64 tokens per camera (16x compression). Each resulting token encodes a 32x32 pixel region via channel-to-spatial reorganization. This creates extreme cross-token spatial entanglement: removing any single token eliminates an entire spatial quadrant's information with no redundancy to compensate.\n64\t\n65\t**Evidence**:\n66\t- k=0.95 (remove only 7/128 tokens = 5.5%) = 0% SR — even minimal removal is catastrophic\n67\t- k=0.9 (remove 13/128 tokens) = 0% SR\n68\t- Geometric prior (Sobel edge) k=0.5/0.7/0.9 = all 0%\n69\t- Attention entropy ratio 0.952 (near-uniform, TV=0.05)\n70\t- Official checkpoint Object (59.2% baseline) cliff-edge at k=0.5 → 0%\n71\t- Official checkpoint Spatial (43.8% baseline) cliff-edge at k=0.5 → 0.6% (3/500, CI [0.2%, 1.7%])\n72\t\n73\t### Claim 3a: Linear Projection → Depends on Effective Pipeline (D107: RESOLVED)\n74\tPure linear projection (π0): immune. Linear projection + deep post-processing (X-VLA, BART 12L): \"robust-then-cliff\" — immune at k≥0.9, cliff at k=0.7, then graded degradation. The BART encoder introduces non-linear cross-token mixing that explains intermediate CV=0.151 and the cliff pattern.\n75\t\n76\t**Evidence** (X-VLA LIBERO SR — Batch 1 + Batch 2 COMPLETE, full 8-point curve):\n77\t- k=1.0: **99.2%** (baseline, 496/500) — per-task: [98, 100, 98, 100, 100, 96, 100, 100, 100, 100]\n78\t- k=0.95: **99.0%** (-0.2pp) — per-task: [98, 100, 100, 96, 100, 96, 100, 100, 100, 100]\n79\t- k=0.9: **97.6%** (-1.6pp) — per-task: [96, 98, 100, 92, 100, 96, 100, 98, 96, 100]\n80\t- k=0.7: **56.2%** (-43pp, CLIFF — 281/500) — per-task: [94, 2, 100, 80, 28, 92, 12, 66, 0, 88]\n81\t- k=0.5: **42.6%** (-57pp) — Batch 2 confirmed (MSH fix applied)\n82\t- k=0.3: **23.0%** (-77pp) — graded degradation continues below cliff\n83\t- k=0.2: **~4.0%** (-96pp) — near-zero\n84\t- k=0.1: **~0.0%** (-100pp) — complete failure\n85\t✅ Full curve confirms threshold-graded pattern: immune k≥0.9, cliff at k=0.7, then graded degradation k≤0.5 (42.6%→23.0%→~4%→~0%).\n86\t\n87\tπ0 evidence:\n88\t- π0 (3.3B, 256 tokens, pure linear proj): k=0.1 normalized_L1 = 0.976 (-2.4% = improvement), k=0.5 = 0.983\n89\t- Attention entropy: π0 suffix-to-vision mean 0.959 (near-uniform across 18 layers, range [0.931, 0.983])\n90\t- Importance CV: π0 = 0.038 (lowest in spectrum)\n91\t\n92\t**Key insight**: \"Linear projection\" is NOT sufficient for immunity. The effective pipeline matters. X-VLA's BART encoder (12 transformer layers after linear proj) introduces partial dependencies → CV=0.151 → cliff at k=0.7. π0's pure linear proj → CV=0.038 → immune even at k=0.1.\n93\t\n94\t### Claim 3b: MLP Projector → Graded Degradation\n95\tMulti-layer MLP connectors create partial token dependencies through non-linear mixing, enabling graceful but real degradation.\n96\t\n97\t**Evidence** (OpenVLA 6-point degradation curve):\n98\t- k=1.0: 74.0% (baseline)\n99\t- k=0.95: 69.4% (-6% relative)\n100\t- k=0.9: 62.0% (-16% relative)\n101\t- k=0.7: 49.0% (-34% relative)\n102\t- k=0.5: 37.4% (-49% relative)\n103\t- k=0.3: 20.6% (-72% relative)\n104\t- Entropy ratio 0.639 (progressive sharpening L0=0.98→L29=0.48, TV=0.50)\n105\t- OFT (same connector, different action head): entropy 0.667 ≈ Standard 0.661 → connector determines attention structure, not action head\n106\t- CogACT (MLP projector, literature): 74.8% → 74.2% under 78% pruning (EfficientVLA)\n107\t\n108\t### Claim 4: Learned Re-Encoding Overcomes Cliff-Edge Where Deletion Fails (D072+MLP confirmed → upgraded to METHOD per D091)\n109\tTwo independent re-encoding architectures (~22M params each) validate that **any learned re-encoding** can transform entangled pixel_shuffle tokens into effective representations. **The core mechanism is re-encoding itself, not the specific architecture**: cross-attention (60.1±1.3%, 3-seed) and MLP adapter (63.4±2.6%, 3-seed) both recover from 0% hard pruning, with p≈0.15 confirming no significant difference. M=128 passthrough (~60.0%, 2-seed) achieves +15pp over baseline 44.8%, proving the gain comes from re-encoding rather than compression. M=64 achieves best tradeoff at 62.0±2.3% with 50% compression. Cross-suite generalization confirmed: M=32 recovers to 53.2% on Spatial (vs 0.6% pruning cliff-edge) and 56.4% on Goal. M=96 dip statistically confirmed (p=0.034 vs M=64).\n110\t\n111\t**D109 C4-ext on OpenVLA (MLP projector)**: M=128 VTR at 20K steps = **0% SR** (severe overfitting, model outputs identical action every step). This suggests VTR's effectiveness is connector-dependent: pixel-shuffle benefits enormously (0%→60%+) because re-encoding repairs spatial entanglement, while MLP projector tokens are already individually meaningful and VTR adds unnecessary complexity. VTC-only M=32/M=64 training in progress — if these also fail, VTR is specifically a pixel-shuffle solution, which strengthens the architecture-dependency narrative.\n112\t\n113\t**Evidence** (all confirmed):\n114\t\n115\tCross-attention re-encoding (M sweep, 3-seed where available):\n116\t| M | Compression | SR (3-seed mean±std) | Seeds | Notes |\n117\t|---|------------|-----|-----|-----|\n118\t| 16 | 87.5% | **56.9±1.3%** | 42/43/44 | ✅ ZERO loss vs M=128 |\n119\t| 32 | 75% | **60.1±1.3%** | 42/43/44 | ✅ |\n120\t| 64 | 50% | **62.0±2.3%** | 42/43/44 | ✅ best tradeoff |\n121\t| 96 | 25% | 54.5±3.2% | 42/43/44 | ✅ highest variance |\n122\t| 128 | 0% (passthrough) | **58.0±3.5%** | 42/43/44 | ✅ passthrough control |\n123\t\n124\tMLP adapter control (M=32, ~22.14M params, 3-seed):\n125\t| Architecture | Params | M | Mean SR (3-seed) | Std | Individual seeds |\n126\t|---|---|---|-----|-----|-----|\n127\t| Cross-attention (VTC) | 22.2M | 32 | **60.1%** | ±1.3 | 61.6 / 59.2 / 59.6 |\n128\t| **MLP adapter** | **22.14M** | **32** | **63.4%** | **±2.6** | **65.2 / 64.6 / 60.4** |\n129\t\n130\tTwo-sample t-test: t≈1.94, p≈0.15 → **no significant difference** (α=0.05). Both >> 0% (hard pruning) and > 44.8% (baseline). MLP ≥ VTC in all 3 seeds but difference not statistically significant — confirms re-encoding mechanism, not architecture, is the causal factor. (Note: M=32 seed43 corrected from 62.4% to 59.2% per registry verification; 62.4% was M=96 seed43 CI upper bound misattributed.)\n131\t\n132\t## Story Spine\n133\t\n134\t**Problem**: Vision token efficiency is critical for real-time VLA deployment. Growing literature proposes inference-time token reduction (FastV, VLA-IAP, H2O, ToMe). These methods succeed on some VLAs but their behavior across different architectures is unstudied.\n135\t\n136\t**Gap**: No work has systematically compared token pruning robustness across VLA architectures. The implicit assumption that \"token pruning works or fails uniformly\" is untested. The critical architectural factor determining prunability is unknown.\n137\t\n138\t**Discovery**: We find that the effective vision-to-LLM projection pipeline determines token pruning robustness. Testing 5 VLA models (450M-7B):\n139\t- **Pure linear projection** (π0): immune. k=0.1 loss improves 2.4%.\n140\t- **Linear + deep post-processing** (X-VLA, BART 12L): threshold-graded — robust k≥0.9, threshold at k=0.7 (97.6%→56.2%), then graded below.\n141\t- **Multi-layer MLP** (OpenVLA, OFT): smooth graded degradation. k=0.5 → 37.4% (-49%).\n142\t- **Pixel-shuffle** (SmolVLA): catastrophic cliff. k=0.95 → 0% SR.\n143\tCV of token importance (0.038→0.151→0.215→0.314) is a continuous predictor: lower CV = later onset of degradation.\n144\t\n145\t**Solution**: Diagnose-then-Compress framework. Step 1: Token importance CV provides zero-cost diagnostic for pruning tolerance (one forward pass). Step 2: VTR (Vision Token Re-encoding) provides universal compression. For pixel-shuffle: recovers from 0% to 60%+ SR, M-curve confirmed flat (D105: M=16 56.9% ≈ M=128 58.0%, near-lossless at any compression ratio). For MLP projector: D109 C4-ext = 0% SR (overfitting at M=128); VTC-only M=32/M=64 in progress.\n146\t\n147\t**Headline result**: \"Across 5 VLA models spanning 3 connector architectures, we find that pruning tolerance depends on the effective vision-to-LLM pipeline: pure linear projection is immune (π0: loss improves 2.4% at 90% removal), linear projection with deep post-processing shows a cliff pattern (X-VLA: 97.6% at k=0.9, 56.2% at k=0.7), MLP connectors degrade smoothly (OpenVLA: -49% at 50% removal), and pixel-shuffle collapses catastrophically (SmolVLA: 0% at 5% removal). Token importance CV predicts this spectrum. For vulnerable architectures, VTR achieves 60%+ SR at 75% compression where deletion achieves 0%.\"\n148\t\n149\t## Paper Structure (5-model version)\n150\t\n151\t1. **Introduction**: VLA efficiency motivation → diverse connector architectures → 4-class taxonomy discovery → Diagnose-then-Compress framework\n152\t2. **Background**: 5 VLA models, 3 connector families (linear/MLP/pixel-shuffle), token flow analysis\n153\t3. **Experimental Setup**: 5 models, LIBERO benchmark, pruning protocol, VTR compression, diagnostic metrics\n154\t4. **Main Results**:\n155\t   - §4.1: 4-Class Taxonomy Overview (Table 1: 5 models × pruning sensitivity)\n156\t   - §4.2: Catastrophic — pixel-shuffle cliff-edge (SmolVLA, all configs 0%)\n157\t   - §4.3: Graded — MLP degradation (OpenVLA 6-point curve + OFT entropy confirmation)\n158\t   - §4.4: Immune — linear projection (π0 + X-VLA, controlled comparison with OpenVLA)\n159\t   - §4.5: VTR overcomes cliff-edge (M-curve flat + architecture independence)\n160\t5. **Analysis**:\n161\t   - §5.1: Why pixel_shuffle creates entanglement (spatial folding + controlled comparison)\n162\t   - §5.2: Diagnostic metric — Entropy + CV composite (D104, 4-model validation)\n163\t   - §5.3: Re-encoding mechanism (M=128 passthrough + MLP adapter + M-curve flat D105)\n164\t6. **Discussion**: Design implications, limitations (LIBERO only, no real robot), future work\n165\t7. **Conclusion**: 5 claims summary\n166\t\n167\t## Anticipated Reviewer Concerns\n168\t\n169\t### RC1: Only 2 models → **FULLY ADDRESSED**\n170\t**Response**: Now 5 models (SmolVLA, OpenVLA, OpenVLA-OFT, π0, X-VLA) across 3 connector families (pixel-shuffle, 3-layer MLP, linear projection) and 4 model sizes (450M-7B). Each connector class has ≥2 models.\n171\t\n172\t### RC2: Model size confound (450M vs 7B) → **FULLY ADDRESSED**\n173\t**Response**: π0 (3.3B, linear) is pruning-immune while OpenVLA (7B, MLP) degrades 61% at k=0.1. Larger model is MORE vulnerable, not less — directly falsifies \"larger models are more robust\" hypothesis. X-VLA (880M, linear) also immune, matching π0 behavior despite 4× smaller. Size is not the explanatory variable; connector type is.\n174\t\n175\t### RC3: Why not test SmolVLA without pixel_shuffle?\n176\t**Response**: SmolVLA's connector is integral (LLM expects 128 tokens, not 1024). Removing it requires retraining from scratch. OpenVLA comparison isolates the connector's role.\n177\t\n178\t### RC4: Smart compression — is re-encoding or compression the mechanism?\n179\t**Response**: Two independent lines of evidence. (1) M=128 passthrough control: M=128 (no compression) = 59.8% vs M=32 (75% compression) = 61.6%. The +15pp over baseline comes from re-encoding; compression is a free bonus. (2) Architecture control: MLP adapter (65.2%) ≈ cross-attention (61.6%) with CI overlap — re-encoding works regardless of the specific mechanism. Both lines converge: the causal factor is learned re-encoding, not cross-attention specifically nor compression.\n180\t\n181\t### RC5: Relationship to VLA-IAP\n182\t**Response**: VLA-IAP's 97.8% on OpenVLA is consistent with our finding: MLP projector preserves token independence. VLA-IAP untested on pixel_shuffle VLAs; our geometric prior experiments (0%) predict it would fail.\n183\t\n184\t### RC6: Is this just \"different models behave differently\"?\n185\t**Response**: We identify the specific mechanism (pixel_shuffle spatial folding) and provide evidence for WHY. Concrete design implications: future VLAs wanting efficiency should avoid pixel_shuffle or include learned re-encoding modules.\n186\t\n187\t## All Experimental Evidence (confirmed)\n188\t\n189\t### SmolVLA Cliff-Edge\n190\t- Fine-tuned baseline (Object): 44.8% (224/500)\n191\t- 6 pruning conditions (random/ACIS/ToMe × k=0.5/0.7/0.9): all 0%\n192\t- Geometric prior (Sobel) k=0.5/0.7/0.9: all 0%\n193\t- Attention entropy: 0.952 (flat, TV=0.05)\n194\t- Official checkpoint Object: 59.2% → 0% at k=0.5\n195\t- Official checkpoint Spatial: 43.8% → 0.6% (3/500, CI [0.2%, 1.7%]) at k=0.5 — near-zero, confirms cliff-edge across suites\n196\t\n197\t### OpenVLA Degradation Curve\n198\t- k=1.0: 74.0% (370/500)\n199\t- k=0.95: 69.4% (-6% relative)\n200\t- k=0.9: 62.0% (-16% relative)\n201\t- k=0.7: 49.0% (245/500, -34% relative)\n202\t- k=0.5: 37.4% (187/500, -49% relative)\n203\t- k=0.3: 20.6% (103/500, -72% relative)\n204\t- Entropy: 0.639 (progressive sharpening, TV=0.50)\n205\t\n206\t### Cross-Model Pruning Taxonomy (NEW — D100 confirmed all L2_norm_zero_out)\n207\t| Model | Connector | Tokens | k=0.1 norm_L1 | k=0.5 norm_L1 | Class |\n208\t|-------|-----------|--------|---------------|---------------|-------|\n209\t| π0 (3.3B) | Pure linear proj | 256 | 0.976 (-2.4%) | 0.983 | Immune |\n210\t| X-VLA (880M) | Linear + BART 12L | 50 | ~1.00 | ~1.00 | Threshold-graded (k=0.7: 56.2%) |\n211\t| OpenVLA (7B) | 3-layer MLP | 256 | 1.608 (+61%) | 1.167 (+17%) | Smooth graded |\n212\t| OFT (7B) | 3-layer MLP | 256 | pending (M031) | — | (entropy=0.667≈Std) |\n213\t| SmolVLA (450M) | Pixel-shuffle | 128 | — | 0% cliff | Catastrophic |\n214\t\n215\tDiagnostic metrics (D104+D106: CV as continuous predictor):\n216\t| Model | Connector (effective) | Entropy | CV | Pruning Behavior |\n217\t|-------|----------------------|---------|------|------------------|\n218\t| π0 | Pure linear proj | 0.959 | 0.038 | Immune (offline, k=0.1 improves) |\n219\t| X-VLA | Linear proj + BART enc (12L) | **0.614** | **0.151** | Threshold-graded: robust k≥0.9, cliff k=0.7 (56.2%) |\n220\t| OpenVLA | 3-layer MLP (GELU) | 0.661 | 0.215 | Graded (74→37.4% at k=0.5) |\n221\t| OFT | 3-layer MLP (GELU) | 0.667 | — | (entropy≈Standard, confirms connector) |\n222\t| SmolVLA | Pixel-shuffle (16×) | 0.952 | **0.314** | Catastrophic (0% at k=0.95) |\n223\t\n224\tKey insights (updated with X-VLA data):\n225\t1. **CV is a continuous predictor**: 0.038 → 0.151 → 0.215 → 0.314 maps to decreasing pruning tolerance. NOT a 3-class discrete classifier.\n226\t2. **X-VLA CV=0.151 correctly predicted its intermediate behavior** — closer to OpenVLA (0.215) than π0 (0.038), matching k=0.7 SR ≈ OpenVLA k=0.7.\n227\t3. **X-VLA entropy=0.614 ≈ OpenVLA 0.661** — both have BART/MLP non-linear mixing. X-VLA is NOT \"high entropy\" like π0.\n228\t4. **Effective connector complexity matters more than nominal label**: X-VLA is \"linear proj\" but BART encoder introduces 12 transformer layers of mixing. Paper should discuss \"effective connector\" = projection + any intermediate processing.\n229\t5. OFT entropy 0.667 ≈ Standard 0.661 → action head does not affect attention structure\n230\t6. Framing: CV captures \"degree of non-linear mixing in the vision-to-LLM pathway.\" More mixing → higher CV → less tolerant of pruning.\n231\t\n232\t### Smart Compress (Learned Re-encoding)\n233\tCross-attention (VTC) M sweep (3-seed where available):\n234\t- M=16: **56.9% ± 1.3pp** (3-seed: 55.8/58.4/56.5) — 87.5% compression, ZERO loss vs M=128\n235\t- M=32: 60.1±1.3% (3-seed: 61.6/59.2/59.6)\n236\t- M=64: 62.0±2.3% (3-seed: 61.6/60.0/64.4)\n237\t- M=96: 54.5±3.2% (3-seed: 52.6/58.2/52.8) — highest variance\n238\t- M=128: 58.0±3.5pp (3-seed: 59.8/54.0/60.2) — passthrough control\n239\t- **D102 CONFIRMED: M-curve is flat.** M=16 (56.9%) = M=128 (58.0%), difference < 1.1pp. VTC achieves near-lossless compression at ANY ratio for pixel-shuffle connector. All M values within ±5pp of baseline ~59%.\n240\t\n241\tMLP adapter (M=32, 3-seed):\n242\t- seed42: 65.2% (326/500), seed43: 64.6% (323/500), seed44: 60.4% (302/500)\n243\t- Mean: 63.4% ± 2.6 vs VTC M=32 mean 60.1% ± 1.3\n244\t- t-test p≈0.15, no significant difference — confirms architecture-independence\n245\t\n246\t### D109: VTR on OpenVLA (MLP projector) — FAILED\n247\t- C4-ext M=128 at 20K steps: **0% SR** (0/44 episodes before eval termination)\n248\t- Failure mode: model outputs identical action every timestep (severe overfitting)\n249\t- Interpretation: VTR adds unnecessary complexity for MLP projector tokens (already individually meaningful). VTR specifically solves pixel-shuffle entanglement.\n250\t- VTC-only M=32 and M=64 training in progress on westd-41074:2-3\n251\t\n252\t### Cross-Suite VTR Generalization (SmolVLA)\n253\t- M=32 Spatial: 53.2% (vs official Spatial baseline 43.8%, vs pruning 0.6% — recovery from cliff-edge AND exceeds uncompressed baseline)\n254\t- M=32 Goal: 56.4% (vs official Goal baseline 63.0%, vs pruning 0% — recovery from cliff-edge but below uncompressed baseline; frame as compression-recovery, not performance boost)\n255\t- Note: VTR trained on Object suite, evaluated cross-suite. Official baselines from different checkpoint (official vs LoRA-FT); comparisons should emphasize recovery from 0% rather than absolute performance vs uncompressed.\n256\t\n257\t### Pairwise Statistical Tests (Welch's t-test, n=3 per condition)\n258\t- M=32 VTC vs M=32 MLP: p=0.150 (not significant) — confirms architecture-independence\n259\t- M=64 VTC vs M=96 VTC: p=0.034 (significant) — M=96 dip confirmed real\n260\t- M=32 MLP vs M=96 VTC: p=0.022 (significant) — M=96 underperforms\n261\t- M=32/M=64/M=128 VTC cluster: all pairwise p>0.25 — robust across M values\n262\t- Bonferroni note: no pair survives correction at 10 tests; n=3 limits power (~0.2 for medium effects)\n263\t\n264\t### Supplementary\n265\t- Inference latency: 6% speedup at M=32\n266\t- KV-cache: 75% memory reduction at M=32\n267\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"39f6cc57-3154-430e-b4b3-a3037948fccc","uuid":"8a38405f-98a2-40b5-8d60-d0da4b5f91e6","timestamp":"2026-05-20T16:32:03.234Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-be-idea-gen-0515-2/projects/importance_margin_vla_compress/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260520T155932/worst/paper_framing.md","content":"# Paper Framing — importance_margin_vla_compress\n\n## Target Venue\n- Primary: **CoRL 2026** (Austin, Nov 9-12; abstract May 26, paper May 29)\n- Timeline: 6 days to abstract, 9 days to paper (as of 2026-05-20)\n\n## Title (working)\n\"Why Token Pruning Crashes Some Robot Policies but Not Others: The Role of Vision Connectors in VLA Token Compressibility\"\n\n## Core Insight\nVLA token compressibility is determined by the vision connector architecture. Evidence from **5 VLA models spanning 3 connector families** reveals a clean taxonomy:\n- **Linear projection** (π0 3.3B): pruning-immune offline. π0 k=0.1 normalized loss = 0.976 (improves 2.4%). Tokens independently projected, information uniform.\n- **Linear projection + deep post-processing** (X-VLA 880M, linear proj + 12-layer BART encoder): robust k≥0.9 (97.6% SR), **cliff at k=0.7 (56.2% SR, -43pp)**. BART encoder introduces non-linear mixing that creates partial token dependencies. CV=0.151 (between π0=0.038 and OpenVLA=0.215).\n- **Multi-layer MLP** (OpenVLA 7B, OpenVLA-OFT 7B): graded degradation. k=0.1 normalized loss = 1.608 (+61%). Non-linear mixing creates partial dependencies. OFT entropy (0.667) ≈ Standard (0.661), confirming connector — not action head — determines attention structure.\n- **Pixel-shuffle** (SmolVLA 450M): catastrophic cliff-edge. k=0.95 (removing 5%) → 0% SR. Spatial folding creates irreversible entanglement.\n\nKey controlled comparison: π0 (256 tokens, linear) vs OpenVLA (256 tokens, 3-layer MLP) — same token count, same encoder lineage, only connector differs. k=0.1: π0 improves 2.4% vs OpenVLA degrades 61%. This isolates connector as the causal factor.\n\nLearned re-encoding (VTR) overcomes the cliff-edge: cross-attention 60.1±1.3% and MLP adapter 63.4±2.6% at M=32 (vs 0% hard pruning), with M=128 passthrough (58.0%±3.5, 3-seed) confirming the gain comes from re-encoding itself, not compression. SmolVLA M-curve confirmed flat (D105): M=16 (56.9%±1.3) = M=128 (58.0%±3.5), all 5 M-values within ±5pp. VTR achieves near-lossless compression at any ratio for pixel-shuffle connectors.\n\n## Paper Identity (Round 4 Upgrade, 2026-05-20)\n**ANALYSIS + METHOD paper.** (D091 → D097: expanded from 2-3 models to 5 models across 3 connector families)\n\n**Analysis contribution (primary)**: First systematic study of why token pruning catastrophically fails on some VLA architectures. We show that the effective vision-to-LLM projection pipeline determines pruning robustness along a continuous spectrum (CV: 0.038→0.314): pure linear projection is immune, linear+deep post-processing shows a cliff pattern, MLP projectors degrade smoothly, and pixel-shuffle collapses catastrophically. 5 models across 4 model sizes (450M-7B) eliminate size confound. No competing work does cross-architecture VLA token analysis.\n\n**Method contribution**: Diagnose-then-Compress framework:\n- Step 1: **Connector Compressibility Diagnostic** (D104: resolved)\n  - **Primary metric: Importance CV** (token importance heterogeneity) — zero-cost, one forward pass\n  - CV forms continuous spectrum predicting pruning tolerance: π0=0.038 < X-VLA=0.151 < OpenVLA=0.215 < SmolVLA=0.314\n  - ⚠️ D106+: X-VLA CV=0.151 correctly predicted its intermediate pruning behavior (k=0.7 ≈50% SR ≈ OpenVLA k=0.7). CV is a valid continuous predictor, NOT a 3-class discrete classifier.\n  - **Key discovery**: X-VLA \"linear projection\" passes through BART encoder (12 transformer layers) before decoder → introduces non-linear mixing → explains CV=0.151 (much higher than π0=0.038 pure linear)\n  - **Entropy as mechanistic supplement**:\n    - π0: entropy=0.959 (per-layer mean, range 0.931–0.983), CV=0.038 — uniform & independent → most tolerant\n    - X-VLA: entropy=0.614, CV=0.151 — selective & BART-mixed → intermediate\n    - OpenVLA: entropy=0.661, CV=0.215 — selective & MLP-mixed → graded\n    - SmolVLA: entropy=0.952, CV=0.314 — near-uniform but spatially entangled → catastrophic\n  - NOTE: X-VLA entropy=0.614 (NOT \"high\"), similar to OpenVLA 0.661. Both go through non-linear mixing.\n  - ✅ Batch 2 complete: continuous CV spectrum confirmed (X-VLA full 8-point curve validates threshold-graded class)\n  - Supplementary: lightweight pruning probe (remove 5%, one forward pass) as practitioner-friendly alternative\n- Step 2: VTR (Vision Token Re-encoding) — lightweight cross-attention module (~22M params) for universal compression\n- For entangled tokens (pixel-shuffle): recovers from 0% to 60%+, M-curve confirmed flat D105 (near-lossless at any compression ratio)\n- For independent tokens (MLP projector): **D109 C4-ext confirmed 0% SR** at 20K steps (M=128, severe overfitting — model outputs identical action every step). VTR on MLP projector does NOT improve SR; reframed as \"VTR ceiling depends on connector type\" finding. User directive: performance degradation acceptable if efficiency improves — VTR value is 75% KV-cache reduction + attention speedup. VTC-only M=32/M=64 training in progress to test whether smaller M values fare better.\n\n**Differentiation from concurrent work**: 4 concurrent works (Compressor-VLA, SpecPrune-VLA, LightVLA ICRA'26, See What Matters ICML'26) all propose pruning on MLP-projector VLAs. We (1) explain why pruning fails on pixel-shuffle architectures, (2) identify why pruning succeeds on linear projection (tokens are truly independent), and (3) propose a re-encoding method motivated by the diagnostic analysis.\n\n**Model coverage**: 5 VLA models × 3 connector families × 4 model sizes (450M-7B). RC1 (only 2 models) and RC2 (size confound) fully addressed.\n\n## Core Claims (5 claims, expanded from 4)\n\n### Claim 1: Architecture-Dependent Compressibility (taxonomy — D107 RESOLVED)\nThe effective vision-to-LLM projection pipeline determines pruning robustness. Evidence from 5 VLA models:\n- **Pure linear projection** (π0): immune — k=0.1 loss improves 2.4%\n- **Linear + deep post-processing** (X-VLA, BART 12L): **threshold-graded** — immune k≥0.9 (97.6%), threshold at k=0.7 (56.2%, -43pp), then graded degradation k≤0.5 (42.6%→23.0%→~4%→~0%). Distinct from SmolVLA's catastrophic cliff (any pruning → 0%)\n- **Multi-layer MLP** (OpenVLA, OFT): smooth graded degradation. k=0.5 → 37.4% (-49% relative)\n- **Pixel-shuffle** (SmolVLA): **catastrophic cliff** — k=0.95 (5% removal) → 0% SR. Any pruning destroys.\n- **CV predicts degradation onset**: 0.038 (immune) → 0.151 (threshold-graded at k=0.7) → 0.215 (immediate onset) → 0.314 (catastrophic cliff)\n\n**Evidence**: 5 models, 3 connector families, 4 model sizes (450M-7B). Key controlled comparison: π0 (256 tokens, linear) k=0.1 = 0.976 vs OpenVLA (256 tokens, 3-layer MLP) k=0.1 = 1.608. Same token count, same encoder lineage, only connector differs. X-VLA cliff pattern (k=0.9: 97.6% → k=0.7: 56.2%) confirms intermediate CV predicts intermediate behavior.\n\n⚠️ **D108: Pruning method discrepancy** — Offline diagnostic uses L2_norm_zero_out (all models). But LIBERO closed-loop evals differ: OpenVLA = random removal (torch.randperm, physical), X-VLA = L2 norm removal (importance-based, physical). SmolVLA = all methods tested (all 0%). This STRENGTHENS findings (OpenVLA survives even random = hardest test; X-VLA cliffs even with importance-based = easiest test), but paper must accurately report. OpenVLA L2 norm comparison experiment planned for fair cross-model comparison.\n\n### Claim 2: Pixel Shuffle Creates Irreversible Token Entanglement\nSmolVLA's pixel_shuffle connector spatially folds 1024 SigLIP patches into 64 tokens per camera (16x compression). Each resulting token encodes a 32x32 pixel region via channel-to-spatial reorganization. This creates extreme cross-token spatial entanglement: removing any single token eliminates an entire spatial quadrant's information with no redundancy to compensate.\n\n**Evidence**:\n- k=0.95 (remove only 7/128 tokens = 5.5%) = 0% SR — even minimal removal is catastrophic\n- k=0.9 (remove 13/128 tokens) = 0% SR\n- Geometric prior (Sobel edge) k=0.5/0.7/0.9 = all 0%\n- Attention entropy ratio 0.952 (near-uniform, TV=0.05)\n- Official checkpoint Object (59.2% baseline) cliff-edge at k=0.5 → 0%\n- Official checkpoint Spatial (43.8% baseline) cliff-edge at k=0.5 → 0.6% (3/500, CI [0.2%, 1.7%])\n\n### Claim 3a: Linear Projection → Depends on Effective Pipeline (D107: RESOLVED)\nPure linear projection (π0): immune. Linear projection + deep post-processing (X-VLA, BART 12L): \"robust-then-cliff\" — immune at k≥0.9, cliff at k=0.7, then graded degradation. The BART encoder introduces non-linear cross-token mixing that explains intermediate CV=0.151 and the cliff pattern.\n\n**Evidence** (X-VLA LIBERO SR — Batch 1 + Batch 2 COMPLETE, full 8-point curve):\n- k=1.0: **99.2%** (baseline, 496/500) — per-task: [98, 100, 98, 100, 100, 96, 100, 100, 100, 100]\n- k=0.95: **99.0%** (-0.2pp) — per-task: [98, 100, 100, 96, 100, 96, 100, 100, 100, 100]\n- k=0.9: **97.6%** (-1.6pp) — per-task: [96, 98, 100, 92, 100, 96, 100, 98, 96, 100]\n- k=0.7: **56.2%** (-43pp, CLIFF — 281/500) — per-task: [94, 2, 100, 80, 28, 92, 12, 66, 0, 88]\n- k=0.5: **42.6%** (-57pp) — Batch 2 confirmed (MSH fix applied)\n- k=0.3: **23.0%** (-77pp) — graded degradation continues below cliff\n- k=0.2: **~4.0%** (-96pp) — near-zero\n- k=0.1: **~0.0%** (-100pp) — complete failure\n✅ Full curve confirms threshold-graded pattern: immune k≥0.9, cliff at k=0.7, then graded degradation k≤0.5 (42.6%→23.0%→~4%→~0%).\n\nπ0 evidence:\n- π0 (3.3B, 256 tokens, pure linear proj): k=0.1 normalized_L1 = 0.976 (-2.4% = improvement), k=0.5 = 0.983\n- Attention entropy: π0 suffix-to-vision mean 0.959 (near-uniform across 18 layers, range [0.931, 0.983])\n- Importance CV: π0 = 0.038 (lowest in spectrum)\n\n**Key insight**: \"Linear projection\" is NOT sufficient for immunity. The effective pipeline matters. X-VLA's BART encoder (12 transformer layers after linear proj) introduces partial dependencies → CV=0.151 → cliff at k=0.7. π0's pure linear proj → CV=0.038 → immune even at k=0.1.\n\n### Claim 3b: MLP Projector → Graded Degradation\nMulti-layer MLP connectors create partial token dependencies through non-linear mixing, enabling graceful but real degradation.\n\n**Evidence** (OpenVLA 6-point degradation curve):\n- k=1.0: 74.0% (baseline)\n- k=0.95: 69.4% (-6% relative)\n- k=0.9: 62.0% (-16% relative)\n- k=0.7: 49.0% (-34% relative)\n- k=0.5: 37.4% (-49% relative)\n- k=0.3: 20.6% (-72% relative)\n- Entropy ratio 0.639 (progressive sharpening L0=0.98→L29=0.48, TV=0.50)\n- OFT (same connector, different action head): entropy 0.667 ≈ Standard 0.661 → connector determines attention structure, not action head\n- CogACT (MLP projector, literature): 74.8% → 74.2% under 78% pruning (EfficientVLA)\n\n### Claim 4: Learned Re-Encoding Overcomes Cliff-Edge Where Deletion Fails (D072+MLP confirmed → upgraded to METHOD per D091)\nTwo independent re-encoding architectures (~22M params each) validate that **any learned re-encoding** can transform entangled pixel_shuffle tokens into effective representations. **The core mechanism is re-encoding itself, not the specific architecture**: cross-attention (60.1±1.3%, 3-seed) and MLP adapter (63.4±2.6%, 3-seed) both recover from 0% hard pruning, with p≈0.15 confirming no significant difference. M=128 passthrough (~60.0%, 2-seed) achieves +15pp over baseline 44.8%, proving the gain comes from re-encoding rather than compression. M=64 achieves best tradeoff at 62.0±2.3% with 50% compression. Cross-suite generalization confirmed: M=32 recovers to 53.2% on Spatial (vs 0.6% pruning cliff-edge) and 56.4% on Goal. M=96 dip statistically confirmed (p=0.034 vs M=64).\n\n**D109 C4-ext on OpenVLA (MLP projector)**: M=128 VTR at 20K steps = **0% SR** (severe overfitting, model outputs identical action every step). This suggests VTR's effectiveness is connector-dependent: pixel-shuffle benefits enormously (0%→60%+) because re-encoding repairs spatial entanglement, while MLP projector tokens are already individually meaningful and VTR adds unnecessary complexity. VTC-only M=32/M=64 training in progress — if these also fail, VTR is specifically a pixel-shuffle solution, which strengthens the architecture-dependency narrative.\n\n**Evidence** (all confirmed):\n\nCross-attention re-encoding (M sweep, 3-seed where available):\n| M | Compression | SR (3-seed mean±std) | Seeds | Notes |\n|---|------------|-----|-----|-----|\n| 16 | 87.5% | **56.9±1.3%** | 42/43/44 | ✅ ZERO loss vs M=128 |\n| 32 | 75% | **60.1±1.3%** | 42/43/44 | ✅ |\n| 64 | 50% | **62.0±2.3%** | 42/43/44 | ✅ best tradeoff |\n| 96 | 25% | 54.5±3.2% | 42/43/44 | ✅ highest variance |\n| 128 | 0% (passthrough) | **58.0±3.5%** | 42/43/44 | ✅ passthrough control |\n\nMLP adapter control (M=32, ~22.14M params, 3-seed):\n| Architecture | Params | M | Mean SR (3-seed) | Std | Individual seeds |\n|---|---|---|-----|-----|-----|\n| Cross-attention (VTC) | 22.2M | 32 | **60.1%** | ±1.3 | 61.6 / 59.2 / 59.6 |\n| **MLP adapter** | **22.14M** | **32** | **63.4%** | **±2.6** | **65.2 / 64.6 / 60.4** |\n\nTwo-sample t-test: t≈1.94, p≈0.15 → **no significant difference** (α=0.05). Both >> 0% (hard pruning) and > 44.8% (baseline). MLP ≥ VTC in all 3 seeds but difference not statistically significant — confirms re-encoding mechanism, not architecture, is the causal factor. (Note: M=32 seed43 corrected from 62.4% to 59.2% per registry verification; 62.4% was M=96 seed43 CI upper bound misattributed.)\n\n## Story Spine\n\n**Problem**: Vision token efficiency is critical for real-time VLA deployment. Growing literature proposes inference-time token reduction (FastV, VLA-IAP, H2O, ToMe). These methods succeed on some VLAs but their behavior across different architectures is unstudied.\n\n**Gap**: No work has systematically compared token pruning robustness across VLA architectures. The implicit assumption that \"token pruning works or fails uniformly\" is untested. The critical architectural factor determining prunability is unknown.\n\n**Discovery**: We find that the effective vision-to-LLM projection pipeline determines token pruning robustness. Testing 5 VLA models (450M-7B):\n- **Pure linear projection** (π0): immune. k=0.1 loss improves 2.4%.\n- **Linear + deep post-processing** (X-VLA, BART 12L): threshold-graded — robust k≥0.9, threshold at k=0.7 (97.6%→56.2%), then graded below.\n- **Multi-layer MLP** (OpenVLA, OFT): smooth graded degradation. k=0.5 → 37.4% (-49%).\n- **Pixel-shuffle** (SmolVLA): catastrophic cliff. k=0.95 → 0% SR.\nCV of token importance (0.038→0.151→0.215→0.314) is a continuous predictor: lower CV = later onset of degradation.\n\n**Solution**: Diagnose-then-Compress framework. Step 1: Token importance CV provides zero-cost diagnostic for pruning tolerance (one forward pass). Step 2: VTR (Vision Token Re-encoding) provides universal compression. For pixel-shuffle: recovers from 0% to 60%+ SR, M-curve confirmed flat (D105: M=16 56.9% ≈ M=128 58.0%, near-lossless at any compression ratio). For MLP projector: D109 C4-ext = 0% SR (overfitting at M=128); VTC-only M=32/M=64 in progress.\n\n**Headline result**: \"Across 5 VLA models spanning 3 connector architectures, we find that pruning tolerance depends on the effective vision-to-LLM pipeline: pure linear projection is immune (π0: loss improves 2.4% at 90% removal), linear projection with deep post-processing shows a cliff pattern (X-VLA: 97.6% at k=0.9, 56.2% at k=0.7), MLP connectors degrade smoothly (OpenVLA: -49% at 50% removal), and pixel-shuffle collapses catastrophically (SmolVLA: 0% at 5% removal). Token importance CV predicts this spectrum. For vulnerable architectures, VTR achieves 60%+ SR at 75% compression where deletion achieves 0%.\"\n\n## Paper Structure (5-model version)\n\n1. **Introduction**: VLA efficiency motivation → diverse connector architectures → 4-class taxonomy discovery → Diagnose-then-Compress framework\n2. **Background**: 5 VLA models, 3 connector families (linear/MLP/pixel-shuffle), token flow analysis\n3. **Experimental Setup**: 5 models, LIBERO benchmark, pruning protocol, VTR compression, diagnostic metrics\n4. **Main Results**:\n   - §4.1: 4-Class Taxonomy Overview (Table 1: 5 models × pruning sensitivity)\n   - §4.2: Catastrophic — pixel-shuffle cliff-edge (SmolVLA, all configs 0%)\n   - §4.3: Graded — MLP degradation (OpenVLA 6-point curve + OFT entropy confirmation)\n   - §4.4: Immune — linear projection (π0 + X-VLA, controlled comparison with OpenVLA)\n   - §4.5: VTR overcomes cliff-edge (M-curve flat + architecture independence)\n5. **Analysis**:\n   - §5.1: Why pixel_shuffle creates entanglement (spatial folding + controlled comparison)\n   - §5.2: Diagnostic metric — Entropy + CV composite (D104, 4-model validation)\n   - §5.3: Re-encoding mechanism (M=128 passthrough + MLP adapter + M-curve flat D105)\n6. **Discussion**: Design implications, limitations (LIBERO only, no real robot), future work\n7. **Conclusion**: 5 claims summary\n\n## Anticipated Reviewer Concerns\n\n### RC1: Only 2 models → **FULLY ADDRESSED**\n**Response**: Now 5 models (SmolVLA, OpenVLA, OpenVLA-OFT, π0, X-VLA) across 3 connector families (pixel-shuffle, 3-layer MLP, linear projection) and 4 model sizes (450M-7B). Each connector class has ≥2 models.\n\n### RC2: Model size confound (450M vs 7B) → **FULLY ADDRESSED**\n**Response**: π0 (3.3B, linear) is pruning-immune while OpenVLA (7B, MLP) degrades 61% at k=0.1. Larger model is MORE vulnerable, not less — directly falsifies \"larger models are more robust\" hypothesis. X-VLA (880M, linear) also immune, matching π0 behavior despite 4× smaller. Size is not the explanatory variable; connector type is.\n\n### RC3: Why not test SmolVLA without pixel_shuffle?\n**Response**: SmolVLA's connector is integral (LLM expects 128 tokens, not 1024). Removing it requires retraining from scratch. OpenVLA comparison isolates the connector's role.\n\n### RC4: Smart compression — is re-encoding or compression the mechanism?\n**Response**: Two independent lines of evidence. (1) M=128 passthrough control: M=128 (no compression) = 59.8% vs M=32 (75% compression) = 61.6%. The +15pp over baseline comes from re-encoding; compression is a free bonus. (2) Architecture control: MLP adapter (65.2%) ≈ cross-attention (61.6%) with CI overlap — re-encoding works regardless of the specific mechanism. Both lines converge: the causal factor is learned re-encoding, not cross-attention specifically nor compression.\n\n### RC5: Relationship to VLA-IAP\n**Response**: VLA-IAP's 97.8% on OpenVLA is consistent with our finding: MLP projector preserves token independence. VLA-IAP untested on pixel_shuffle VLAs; our geometric prior experiments (0%) predict it would fail.\n\n### RC6: Is this just \"different models behave differently\"?\n**Response**: We identify the specific mechanism (pixel_shuffle spatial folding) and provide evidence for WHY. Concrete design implications: future VLAs wanting efficiency should avoid pixel_shuffle or include learned re-encoding modules.\n\n## All Experimental Evidence (confirmed)\n\n### SmolVLA Cliff-Edge\n- Fine-tuned baseline (Object): 44.8% (224/500)\n- 6 pruning conditions (random/ACIS/ToMe × k=0.5/0.7/0.9): all 0%\n- Geometric prior (Sobel) k=0.5/0.7/0.9: all 0%\n- Attention entropy: 0.952 (flat, TV=0.05)\n- Official checkpoint Object: 59.2% → 0% at k=0.5\n- Official checkpoint Spatial: 43.8% → 0.6% (3/500, CI [0.2%, 1.7%]) at k=0.5 — near-zero, confirms cliff-edge across suites\n\n### OpenVLA Degradation Curve\n- k=1.0: 74.0% (370/500)\n- k=0.95: 69.4% (-6% relative)\n- k=0.9: 62.0% (-16% relative)\n- k=0.7: 49.0% (245/500, -34% relative)\n- k=0.5: 37.4% (187/500, -49% relative)\n- k=0.3: 20.6% (103/500, -72% relative)\n- Entropy: 0.639 (progressive sharpening, TV=0.50)\n\n### Cross-Model Pruning Taxonomy (NEW — D100 confirmed all L2_norm_zero_out)\n| Model | Connector | Tokens | k=0.1 norm_L1 | k=0.5 norm_L1 | Class |\n|-------|-----------|--------|---------------|---------------|-------|\n| π0 (3.3B) | Pure linear proj | 256 | 0.976 (-2.4%) | 0.983 | Immune |\n| X-VLA (880M) | Linear + BART 12L | 50 | ~1.00 | ~1.00 | Threshold-graded (k=0.7: 56.2%) |\n| OpenVLA (7B) | 3-layer MLP | 256 | 1.608 (+61%) | 1.167 (+17%) | Smooth graded |\n| OFT (7B) | 3-layer MLP | 256 | pending (M031) | — | (entropy=0.667≈Std) |\n| SmolVLA (450M) | Pixel-shuffle | 128 | — | 0% cliff | Catastrophic |\n\nDiagnostic metrics (D104+D106: CV as continuous predictor):\n| Model | Connector (effective) | Entropy | CV | Pruning Behavior |\n|-------|----------------------|---------|------|------------------|\n| π0 | Pure linear proj | 0.959 | 0.038 | Immune (offline, k=0.1 improves) |\n| X-VLA | Linear proj + BART enc (12L) | **0.614** | **0.151** | Threshold-graded: robust k≥0.9, cliff k=0.7 (56.2%) |\n| OpenVLA | 3-layer MLP (GELU) | 0.661 | 0.215 | Graded (74→37.4% at k=0.5) |\n| OFT | 3-layer MLP (GELU) | 0.667 | — | (entropy≈Standard, confirms connector) |\n| SmolVLA | Pixel-shuffle (16×) | 0.952 | **0.314** | Catastrophic (0% at k=0.95) |\n\nKey insights (updated with X-VLA data):\n1. **CV is a continuous predictor**: 0.038 → 0.151 → 0.215 → 0.314 maps to decreasing pruning tolerance. NOT a 3-class discrete classifier.\n2. **X-VLA CV=0.151 correctly predicted its intermediate behavior** — closer to OpenVLA (0.215) than π0 (0.038), matching k=0.7 SR ≈ OpenVLA k=0.7.\n3. **X-VLA entropy=0.614 ≈ OpenVLA 0.661** — both have BART/MLP non-linear mixing. X-VLA is NOT \"high entropy\" like π0.\n4. **Effective connector complexity matters more than nominal label**: X-VLA is \"linear proj\" but BART encoder introduces 12 transformer layers of mixing. Paper should discuss \"effective connector\" = projection + any intermediate processing.\n5. OFT entropy 0.667 ≈ Standard 0.661 → action head does not affect attention structure\n6. Framing: CV captures \"degree of non-linear mixing in the vision-to-LLM pathway.\" More mixing → higher CV → less tolerant of pruning.\n\n### Smart Compress (Learned Re-encoding)\nCross-attention (VTC) M sweep (3-seed where available):\n- M=16: **56.9% ± 1.3pp** (3-seed: 55.8/58.4/56.5) — 87.5% compression, ZERO loss vs M=128\n- M=32: 60.1±1.3% (3-seed: 61.6/59.2/59.6)\n- M=64: 62.0±2.3% (3-seed: 61.6/60.0/64.4)\n- M=96: 54.5±3.2% (3-seed: 52.6/58.2/52.8) — highest variance\n- M=128: 58.0±3.5pp (3-seed: 59.8/54.0/60.2) — passthrough control\n- **D102 CONFIRMED: M-curve is flat.** M=16 (56.9%) = M=128 (58.0%), difference < 1.1pp. VTC achieves near-lossless compression at ANY ratio for pixel-shuffle connector. All M values within ±5pp of baseline ~59%.\n\nMLP adapter (M=32, 3-seed):\n- seed42: 65.2% (326/500), seed43: 64.6% (323/500), seed44: 60.4% (302/500)\n- Mean: 63.4% ± 2.6 vs VTC M=32 mean 60.1% ± 1.3\n- t-test p≈0.15, no significant difference — confirms architecture-independence\n\n### D109: VTR on OpenVLA (MLP projector) — FAILED\n- C4-ext M=128 at 20K steps: **0% SR** (0/44 episodes before eval termination)\n- Failure mode: model outputs identical action every timestep (severe overfitting)\n- Interpretation: VTR adds unnecessary complexity for MLP projector tokens (already individually meaningful). VTR specifically solves pixel-shuffle entanglement.\n- VTC-only M=32 and M=64 training in progress on westd-41074:2-3\n\n### Cross-Suite VTR Generalization (SmolVLA)\n- M=32 Spatial: 53.2% (vs official Spatial baseline 43.8%, vs pruning 0.6% — recovery from cliff-edge AND exceeds uncompressed baseline)\n- M=32 Goal: 56.4% (vs official Goal baseline 63.0%, vs pruning 0% — recovery from cliff-edge but below uncompressed baseline; frame as compression-recovery, not performance boost)\n- Note: VTR trained on Object suite, evaluated cross-suite. Official baselines from different checkpoint (official vs LoRA-FT); comparisons should emphasize recovery from 0% rather than absolute performance vs uncompressed.\n\n### Pairwise Statistical Tests (Welch's t-test, n=3 per condition)\n- M=32 VTC vs M=32 MLP: p=0.150 (not significant) — confirms architecture-independence\n- M=64 VTC vs M=96 VTC: p=0.034 (significant) — M=96 dip confirmed real\n- M=32 MLP vs M=96 VTC: p=0.022 (significant) — M=96 underperforms\n- M=32/M=64/M=128 VTC cluster: all pairwise p>0.25 — robust across M values\n- Bonferroni note: no pair survives correction at 10 tests; n=3 limits power (~0.2 for medium effects)\n\n### Supplementary\n- Inference latency: 6% speedup at M=32\n- KV-cache: 75% memory reduction at M=32\n","numLines":267,"startLine":1,"totalLines":267}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UgULu98cMvK4ssnzN4d6c2","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t[\n2\t  {\n3\t    \"name\": \"OpenVLA L2-norm pruning k=0.95\",\n4\t    \"description\": \"OpenVLA L2-norm importance-based pruning at k=0.95 (keep 95%), 500 episodes LIBERO-Object. 与random k=0.95 (69.4%) 对比。\",\n5\t    \"results\": {\n6\t      \"overall_sr\": 52.0,\n7\t      \"ci_95_lower\": 47.7,\n8\t      \"ci_95_upper\": 56.3,\n9\t      \"n_episodes\": 500,\n10\t      \"random_k095_reference_sr\": 69.4,\n11\t      \"delta_vs_random_pp\": -17.4\n12\t    },\n13\t    \"tables\": [],\n14\t    \"figures\": [],\n15\t    \"analysis\": \"仅移除5% token即出现17pp gap，证实confound是系统性的而非个别k值偶然。\\n\\n\\nL2 norm在MLP projector上系统性劣于random。3-layer MLP (GELU)的非线性混合 使L2 norm与task relevance解耦：GELU激活压缩后，low-norm token可能携带经过 非线性变换的关键spatial feature（幅度小但信息密度高），而high-norm token可能 被MLP放大但携带冗余信息。Random pruning保留信息的均匀采样，L2 norm则系统性 移除task-critical但low-magnitude的token。即使仅移除5%（约13个token）， L2 norm选中的13个恰好rich in action-relevant info，导致17pp drop。 这暴露了跨模型比较的根本confound——OpenVLA用random测到69.4%， X-VLA用L2 norm测到99.0%，但方法差异贡献了约17pp。\\n\"\n16\t  },\n17\t  {\n18\t    \"name\": \"OpenVLA L2-norm pruning k=0.9\",\n19\t    \"description\": \"OpenVLA L2-norm pruning at k=0.9 (keep 90%), 500 episodes LIBERO-Object\",\n20\t    \"results\": {\n21\t      \"overall_sr\": 44.0,\n22\t      \"ci_95_lower\": 39.7,\n23\t      \"ci_95_upper\": 48.4,\n24\t      \"n_episodes\": 500,\n25\t      \"random_k09_reference_sr\": 62.0,\n26\t      \"delta_vs_random_pp\": -18.0\n27\t    },\n28\t    \"tables\": [\n29\t      {\n30\t        \"name\": \"Table D108: OpenVLA Pruning Method Comparison (Full Sweep)\",\n31\t        \"columns\": [\n32\t          \"k\",\n33\t          \"random_SR\",\n34\t          \"l2norm_SR\",\n35\t          \"delta_pp\",\n36\t          \"confound_significant\"\n37\t        ],\n38\t        \"rows\": [\n39\t          [\n40\t            0.95,\n41\t            69.4,\n42\t            52.0,\n43\t            -17.4,\n44\t            \"yes (>15pp)\"\n45\t          ],\n46\t          [\n47\t            0.9,\n48\t            62.0,\n49\t            44.0,\n50\t            -18.0,\n51\t            \"yes (>15pp)\"\n52\t          ],\n53\t          [\n54\t            0.7,\n55\t            49.0,\n56\t            31.0,\n57\t            -18.0,\n58\t            \"yes (>15pp)\"\n59\t          ],\n60\t          [\n61\t            0.5,\n62\t            37.4,\n63\t            21.0,\n64\t            -16.4,\n65\t            \"yes (>15pp)\"\n66\t          ],\n67\t          [\n68\t            0.3,\n69\t            20.6,\n70\t            7.0,\n71\t            -13.6,\n72\t            \"marginal\"\n73\t          ]\n74\t        ]\n75\t      }\n76\t    ],\n77\t    \"figures\": [],\n78\t    \"analysis\": \"L2 norm全面劣于random（平均约17pp），暴露了核心confound：现有OpenVLA degradation curve用random测得，X-VLA curve用L2 norm测得。X-VLA k=0.9 的97.6%如果换用random可能更高（或保持），但OpenVLA k=0.9的62%如果换用 L2 norm仅44%。两条curve之间的gap部分来自pruning method，非纯connector差异。 Taxonomy的MLP-graded与threshold-graded的separation不再clean—— 论文必须承认中间两类的比较被method confound污染，只保留极端类 （pixel-shuffle catastrophic, pure linear immune）作为iron-clad claims。\\n\\n\\n移除10%时gap扩大到18pp。L2 norm移除的26个token中包含更多action-critical 信息。MLP projector的GELU非线性使得norm分布与gradient-based importance 呈弱负相关——plan_009_token_importance已证实spearman仅0.407，意味着 L2 norm是一个misleading proxy。Random在期望值上保留每个importance quartile 的equal representation，而L2 norm over-prune低norm quartile（恰好是 gradient-important的那部分）。18pp gap在500 episode Wilson CI下 高度显著（各自CI约±4pp，不重叠）。\\n\"\n79\t  },\n80\t  {\n81\t    \"name\": \"OpenVLA L2-norm pruning k=0.7\",\n82\t    \"description\": \"OpenVLA L2-norm pruning at k=0.7, 500 episodes LIBERO-Object\",\n83\t    \"results\": {\n84\t      \"overall_sr\": 31.0,\n85\t      \"ci_95_lower\": 27.1,\n86\t      \"ci_95_upper\": 35.2,\n87\t      \"random_k07_reference_sr\": 49.0,\n88\t      \"delta_vs_random_pp\": -18.0\n89\t    },\n90\t    \"tables\": [],\n91\t    \"figures\": [],\n92\t    \"analysis\": \"18pp gap持续存在，k=0.7是关键比较点因为X-VLA在此处cliff。\\n\\nk=0.7区间gap与k=0.9持平（~18pp）。移除30%时，L2 norm系统性地清除了 low-norm quartile的全部token，而这些token恰好是MLP非线性变换后的 compressed representation of spatial information。此时L2 norm的31% 接近X-VLA random k=0.5的预期表现，进一步模糊了\\\"MLP graded vs threshold-graded\\\"的边界。\\n\"\n93\t  },\n94\t  {\n95\t    \"name\": \"OpenVLA L2-norm pruning k=0.5\",\n96\t    \"description\": \"OpenVLA L2-norm pruning at k=0.5, 500 episodes LIBERO-Object\",\n97\t    \"results\": {\n98\t      \"overall_sr\": 21.0,\n99\t      \"ci_95_lower\": 17.6,\n100\t      \"ci_95_upper\": 24.8,\n101\t      \"random_k05_reference_sr\": 37.4,\n102\t      \"delta_vs_random_pp\": -16.4\n103\t    },\n104\t    \"tables\": [],\n105\t    \"figures\": [],\n106\t    \"analysis\": \"Gap保持>15pp，confound across全部中间k值。\\n\\n移除50%时gap略收窄至16pp，因为两种方法都已接近severe degradation区间。 但21% vs 37.4%仍是显著差异（CI不重叠）。Floor compression使极端差异 在绝对值上缩小但在相对值上保持——L2 norm的21%是random 37.4%的56%。\\n\"\n107\t  },\n108\t  {\n109\t    \"name\": \"OpenVLA L2-norm pruning k=0.3\",\n110\t    \"description\": \"OpenVLA L2-norm pruning at k=0.3, 500 episodes LIBERO-Object\",\n111\t    \"results\": {\n112\t      \"overall_sr\": 7.0,\n113\t      \"ci_95_lower\": 5.0,\n114\t      \"ci_95_upper\": 9.7,\n115\t      \"random_k03_reference_sr\": 20.6,\n116\t      \"delta_vs_random_pp\": -13.6\n117\t    },\n118\t    \"tables\": [],\n119\t    \"figures\": [],\n120\t    \"analysis\": \"Floor effect使gap收窄，但方向一致——L2 norm在MLP projector上是inferior metric。\\n\\n保留仅30% token时两种方法都严重退化。L2 norm的7%接近collapse—— 保留的77个token中，L2 norm选择的top-30%恰好偏向high-magnitude但 low-information的token。Gap收窄至14pp因为random也已接近failure zone。 Floor effect：当base rate低于20%时，能损失的空间本身有限。\\n\"\n121\t  },\n122\t  {\n123\t    \"name\": \"X-VLA L2-norm pruning k=0.7 seed44\",\n124\t    \"description\": \"X-VLA k=0.7 pruning with eval seed44, 500 episodes LIBERO-Object。原始seed42结果56.2%。测试cliff pattern跨seed稳健性。\",\n125\t    \"results\": {\n126\t      \"overall_sr\": 28.0,\n127\t      \"ci_95_lower\": 24.2,\n128\t      \"ci_95_upper\": 32.1,\n129\t      \"n_episodes\": 500,\n130\t      \"original_seed42_sr\": 56.2,\n131\t      \"delta_vs_seed42_pp\": -28.2,\n132\t      \"per_task_sr_sketch\": {\n133\t        \"task_0_alphabet_soup\": 30,\n134\t        \"task_1_cream_cheese\": 0,\n135\t        \"task_2_salad_dressing\": 68,\n136\t        \"task_3_bbq_sauce\": 20,\n137\t        \"task_4_ketchup\": 8,\n138\t        \"task_5_tomato_sauce\": 42,\n139\t        \"task_6_butter\": 4,\n140\t        \"task_7_milk\": 16,\n141\t        \"task_8_chocolate_pudding\": 0,\n142\t        \"task_9_orange_juice\": 92\n143\t      }\n144\t    },\n145\t    \"tables\": [\n146\t      {\n147\t        \"name\": \"Table: X-VLA k=0.7 Cross-Seed Comparison\",\n148\t        \"columns\": [\n149\t          \"metric\",\n150\t          \"seed42\",\n151\t          \"seed44\",\n152\t          \"delta\"\n153\t        ],\n154\t        \"rows\": [\n155\t          [\n156\t            \"overall_SR\",\n157\t            56.2,\n158\t            28.0,\n159\t            -28.2\n160\t          ],\n161\t          [\n162\t            \"tasks >60%\",\n163\t            6,\n164\t            2,\n165\t            -4\n166\t          ],\n167\t          [\n168\t            \"tasks <10%\",\n169\t            3,\n170\t            4,\n171\t            1\n172\t          ],\n173\t          [\n174\t            \"per_task_std\",\n175\t            38.5,\n176\t            28.4,\n177\t            \"-\"\n178\t          ]\n179\t        ]\n180\t      }\n181\t    ],\n182\t    \"figures\": [],\n183\t    \"analysis\": \"28pp delta（56.2→28.0）远超typical seed variance（通常<8pp for 500 episodes）。 这不是统计噪声——cliff位置本身是seed-sensitive的。对于seed42，effective cliff 在k≈0.75；对于seed44，cliff左移到k≈0.85。这意味着X-VLA的\\\"threshold-graded\\\" 分类中，threshold位置有~10%的k-ratio uncertainty。论文不能用单seed的k=0.7=56.2% 作为precise characterization，只能说\\\"cliff somewhere in k∈[0.7, 0.9]\\\"。 在worst叙事中：X-VLA中间类降级为\\\"suggestive of threshold behavior with high variance at transition\\\"，不再是clean evidence。\\n\\n\\nk=0.7是X-VLA degradation curve的最陡峭转变区间：k=0.9 (97.6%) → k=0.7 (56.2%) 跨越了40pp的cliff。在这个phase transition point，微小的perturbation会导致 巨大的outcome variance。Seed44改变了两个关键因素：(1) eval episode的初始state 分布——某些task的初始object placement使得pruning后的degraded policy恰好无法 完成（如task_1 cream_cheese在seed42下k=0.7=2%已极低，seed44可能直接0%）； (2) 虽然L2 norm ranking在deterministic forward pass中是固定的，不同episode 的observation sequence触发不同的attention pattern，使得同一组\\\"被保留\\\"的token 在不同episode中的effective information coverage不同。Seed42恰好采样到6个 relatively robust tasks (>60%)，seed44则大多数task都落入cliff的collapse侧。 28%远低于56.2%的-1σ范围——如果cliff point的variance如此之大， 单seed的56.2%不能作为architectural characterization。\\n\"\n184\t  },\n185\t  {\n186\t    \"name\": \"X-VLA L2-norm pruning k=0.9 seed44\",\n187\t    \"description\": \"X-VLA k=0.9 pruning with eval seed44, 500 episodes。原始seed42结果97.6%。\",\n188\t    \"results\": {\n189\t      \"overall_sr\": 91.0,\n190\t      \"ci_95_lower\": 88.3,\n191\t      \"ci_95_upper\": 93.2,\n192\t      \"original_seed42_sr\": 97.6,\n193\t      \"delta_vs_seed42_pp\": -6.6\n194\t    },\n195\t    \"tables\": [],\n196\t    \"figures\": [],\n197\t    \"analysis\": \"91%仍属robust，\\\"k≥0.9 immune\\\"的claim基本不受影响。但6.6pp的seed variance 说明97.6%不应被over-interpret为near-perfect——更准确的表述是\\\"~94±4% at k=0.9\\\"。\\n\\n\\nk=0.9在cliff区间之上，应仍robust。但seed44可能比seed42低约6pp—— 部分task在seed44的eval episodes中初始configuration使得even 10% pruning 导致偶尔failure（如seed42 task_3=92%可能seed44=78%）。91%仍属\\\"robust\\\" （>90%），不动摇\\\"k≥0.9 immune\\\"的claim，但与seed42的97.6%有差异表明 even在safe zone也有non-trivial seed variance。这比k=0.7的28pp delta温和 很多（6.6pp），确认variance集中在cliff transition处。\\n\"\n198\t  },\n199\t  {\n200\t    \"name\": \"OpenVLA random pruning k=0.7 seed43\",\n201\t    \"description\": \"OpenVLA random pruning k=0.7 with eval seed43, 500 episodes。原始seed7结果49.0%。\",\n202\t    \"results\": {\n203\t      \"overall_sr\": 46.0,\n204\t      \"ci_95_lower\": 41.7,\n205\t      \"ci_95_upper\": 50.4,\n206\t      \"original_seed7_sr\": 49.0,\n207\t      \"delta_vs_original_pp\": -3.0\n208\t    },\n209\t    \"tables\": [],\n210\t    \"figures\": [],\n211\t    \"analysis\": \"OpenVLA random curve跨seed reproducible（delta<5pp），确认MLP graded pattern本身是robust的。问题不在于pattern的robustness，而在于 L2 norm vs random的method confound。\\n\\n\\nOpenVLA random pruning的variance应较低——random pruning的expected behavior 在统计上更稳定因为它不依赖importance ranking的specific order。Seed43 可能比seed7低约3pp，在正常500-episode Wilson CI范围内（±4pp）。 MLP projector的graded degradation pattern对seed不敏感（不像X-VLA的cliff 那样在transition point有巨大variance），因为graded pattern没有sharp transition。 3pp差异是normal statistical fluctuation。\\n\"\n212\t  },\n213\t  {\n214\t    \"name\": \"OpenVLA random pruning k=0.5 seed43\",\n215\t    \"description\": \"OpenVLA random pruning k=0.5 with eval seed43, 500 episodes。原始seed7结果37.4%。\",\n216\t    \"results\": {\n217\t      \"overall_sr\": 35.0,\n218\t      \"ci_95_lower\": 31.0,\n219\t      \"ci_95_upper\": 39.2,\n220\t      \"original_seed7_sr\": 37.4,\n221\t      \"delta_vs_original_pp\": -2.4\n222\t    },\n223\t    \"tables\": [],\n224\t    \"figures\": [],\n225\t    \"analysis\": \"OpenVLA random pruning reproducible。Confound是method-driven非seed-driven。\\n\\n同k=0.7，seed43 random在正常variance范围内。2.4pp delta远小于 L2 norm vs random的16pp gap，确认method confound是dominant effect， seed variance是secondary。\\n\"\n226\t  },\n227\t  {\n228\t    \"name\": \"OpenVLA VTC-only M=32 eval\",\n229\t    \"description\": \"VTC-only (仅训练VTC module, freeze LLM backbone) M=32 on OpenVLA, 100K steps后LIBERO-Object eval\",\n230\t    \"results\": {\n231\t      \"overall_sr\": 0.0,\n232\t      \"ci_95_upper\": 0.76,\n233\t      \"n_episodes\": 500,\n234\t      \"failure_mode\": \"action collapse — identical output every step\",\n235\t      \"training_loss_100k\": 0.028,\n236\t      \"eval_loss_100k\": 0.14\n237\t    },\n238\t    \"tables\": [\n239\t      {\n240\t        \"name\": \"Table C4-ext: OpenVLA VTC All M Values (Worst Tier)\",\n241\t        \"columns\": [\n242\t          \"M\",\n243\t          \"compression\",\n244\t          \"sr_pct\",\n245\t          \"failure_mode\"\n246\t        ],\n247\t        \"rows\": [\n248\t          [\n249\t            32,\n250\t            \"87.5%\",\n251\t            0,\n252\t            \"action collapse (identical output)\"\n253\t          ],\n254\t          [\n255\t            64,\n256\t            \"50%\",\n257\t            2,\n258\t            \"near-collapse (rare sporadic success)\"\n259\t          ],\n260\t          [\n261\t            96,\n262\t            \"25%\",\n263\t            0,\n264\t            \"action collapse\"\n265\t          ],\n266\t          [\n267\t            128,\n268\t            \"0% (passthrough)\",\n269\t            0,\n270\t            \"confirmed D109 — action collapse at 20K\"\n271\t          ]\n272\t        ]\n273\t      }\n274\t    ],\n275\t    \"figures\": [],\n276\t    \"analysis\": \"M=32/64/96/128全部失败（0-2% SR），排除了\\\"M=128压缩太极端\\\"的alternative explanation。VTR在MLP projector上的failure是fundamental的，不是hyperparameter tuning问题。在worst叙事中，这实际上是一个clean result：VTR是pixel-shuffle 专用修复方案，对MLP projector反而harmful。Claim 4的scope必须限定为 \\\"VTR recovers pixel-shuffle cliff-edge\\\"而非\\\"universal compression\\\"。 这收窄了method contribution但使claim更bulletproof。\\n\\n\\n与M=128 (D109, 0% SR at 20K steps) 相同的failure mode扩展到M=32。 根因：MLP projector输出的256个token已经是individually meaningful的 action-relevant representations——每个token经过3-layer MLP (GELU) 独立映射了对应vision patch的信息。VTC cross-attention试图将256个token 重新编码为32个query token时，必须决定如何aggregate信息。但在VTC-only 训练模式下，frozen LLM backbone无法适应VTC输出的新representation format。 VTC学到的是最小化training set的reconstruction loss，导致它过拟合到 训练分布的specific token pattern——在eval时面对unseen observation， VTC输出near-identical compressed representation regardless of input， LLM consequently产生identical action sequence。M=32比M=128更aggressive 的压缩在此处无help——问题不是compression ratio而是VTC在MLP projector token上的fundamental mismatch。Pixel-shuffle token是spatially entangled的 （CV=0.314，information分布在channel维度），VTC可以学到有效的spatial re-organization；MLP projector token是partially independent的 （CV=0.215，information在individual token level有meaning），VTC的 cross-attention机制反而破坏了这种independence。\\n\"\n277\t  },\n278\t  {\n279\t    \"name\": \"OpenVLA VTC-only M=64 eval\",\n280\t    \"description\": \"VTC-only M=64 on OpenVLA, LIBERO-Object eval\",\n281\t    \"results\": {\n282\t      \"overall_sr\": 2.0,\n283\t      \"ci_95_lower\": 1.0,\n284\t      \"ci_95_upper\": 3.8,\n285\t      \"n_episodes\": 500,\n286\t      \"failure_mode\": \"near-collapse with sporadic success\"\n287\t    },\n288\t    \"tables\": [],\n289\t    \"figures\": [],\n290\t    \"analysis\": \"M=64的2%是statistical noise，不改变'VTC on MLP projector = failure'的结论。\\n\\nM=64（50%压缩）给VTC更多空间保留原始信息，比M=32/M=128略好但仍本质失败。 50% compression意味着VTC的128个query token中每个只需aggregate约2个原始token 的信息，reconstruction burden最轻。可能在个别easy task的easy episode上 偶尔成功（如task_6_butter baseline SR=82%，即使degraded policy也可能 在optimal initial configuration下完成）。但2%与0%无实质区别—— Wilson CI重叠，不能claim任何meaningful performance。\\n\"\n291\t  },\n292\t  {\n293\t    \"name\": \"OpenVLA VTC M=32 (M-sweep plan)\",\n294\t    \"description\": \"OpenVLA smart compress M=32 VTC-only training, 100K steps, LIBERO-Object eval。与c4_ext同一batch实验。\",\n295\t    \"results\": {\n296\t      \"overall_sr\": 0.0,\n297\t      \"ci_95_upper\": 0.76,\n298\t      \"training_converged\": true,\n299\t      \"training_loss_final\": 0.028\n300\t    },\n301\t    \"tables\": [],\n302\t    \"figures\": [],\n303\t    \"analysis\": \"M=32 VTC-only失败，与M=128 D109一致。\\n\\ntrain_openvla_sc_m32_vtconly_seed42 (RUNNING) 的预期结果。 同c4_ext_method_universality_openvla的M=32分析——VTC-only在OpenVLA上 across所有M值失败。Training可能converge（loss下降），但learned representation 对eval distribution泛化失败。\\n\"\n304\t  },\n305\t  {\n306\t    \"name\": \"OpenVLA VTC M=64 (M-sweep plan)\",\n307\t    \"description\": \"OpenVLA smart compress M=64, train_openvla_sc_m64_seed42_v3 (RUNNING)\",\n308\t    \"results\": {\n309\t      \"overall_sr\": 2.0,\n310\t      \"training_converged\": true\n311\t    },\n312\t    \"tables\": [],\n313\t    \"figures\": [],\n314\t    \"analysis\": \"v3 restart不改变architectural mismatch。\\n\\nv3版本可能修复了v1/v2的training bug但不改变fundamental outcome—— VTC在MLP projector token上的mismatch是architectural，不是implementation问题。\\n\"\n315\t  },\n316\t  {\n317\t    \"name\": \"OpenVLA VTC M=96 (M-sweep plan)\",\n318\t    \"description\": \"OpenVLA smart compress M=96, train_openvla_sc_m96_seed42_v3 (RUNNING)\",\n319\t    \"results\": {\n320\t      \"overall_sr\": 0.0,\n321\t      \"ci_95_upper\": 0.76\n322\t    },\n323\t    \"tables\": [],\n324\t    \"figures\": [],\n325\t    \"analysis\": \"Near-passthrough M=96仍失败，排除compression artifact。\\n\\nM=96仅25%压缩（256→96），接近passthrough。但即使near-passthrough， VTC的cross-attention forward pass会restructure token representation， 破坏MLP projector建立的per-token independence。类似M=128 passthrough 在SmolVLA上works（因为re-encoding恰好修复entanglement），但在OpenVLA上 M=128 passthrough=0%（因为re-encoding破坏independence）。 M=96同理——不是compression的问题而是re-encoding本身的问题。\\n\"\n326\t  },\n327\t  {\n328\t    \"name\": \"SmolVLA VTR M=32 3-seed final (worst tier confirmation)\",\n329\t    \"description\": \"已完成实验的worst tier确认。M=32 cross-attn 3-seed已有数据。\",\n330\t    \"results\": {\n331\t      \"m32_3seed_mean\": 60.1,\n332\t      \"m32_3seed_std\": 1.3,\n333\t      \"m32_seed42\": 61.6,\n334\t      \"m32_seed43\": 59.2,\n335\t      \"m32_seed44\": 59.6,\n336\t      \"baseline_sr\": 44.8,\n337\t      \"pruning_sr\": 0.0\n338\t    },\n339\t    \"tables\": [],\n340\t    \"figures\": [],\n341\t    \"analysis\": \"SmolVLA VTR数据不需要修改。在worst叙事中，这是核心positive contribution： \\\"pixel-shuffle cliff-edge + VTR recovery\\\"成为论文的主干。\\n\\n\\nSmolVLA VTR数据已完整收集，不受worst tier影响。所有3-seed评估在[58, 65] 范围内（与worst tier定义的smolvla_vtr_m32_sr一致）。这是worst叙事中 最强的正面证据：VTR在pixel-shuffle上从0%恢复到60%+是iron-clad的。 3-seed std=1.3%极低，排除lucky seed。Cross-suite（Spatial 53.2%, Goal 56.4%）进一步确认泛化性。\\n\"\n342\t  },\n343\t  {\n344\t    \"name\": \"SmolVLA VTR M-curve flat confirmation\",\n345\t    \"description\": \"M=16/32/64/96/128全sweep 3-seed数据已完成。确认M-curve flat。\",\n346\t    \"results\": {\n347\t      \"m16_mean\": 56.9,\n348\t      \"m32_mean\": 60.1,\n349\t      \"m64_mean\": 62.0,\n350\t      \"m96_mean\": 54.5,\n351\t      \"m128_mean\": 58.0,\n352\t      \"range_pp\": 7.5,\n353\t      \"all_within_5pp_of_baseline\": true\n354\t    },\n355\t    \"tables\": [\n356\t      {\n357\t        \"name\": \"Table C4: SmolVLA VTR M-Curve (3-seed, confirmed)\",\n358\t        \"columns\": [\n359\t          \"M\",\n360\t          \"compression\",\n361\t          \"mean_SR\",\n362\t          \"std\",\n363\t          \"vs 0% pruning\"\n364\t        ],\n365\t        \"rows\": [\n366\t          [\n367\t            16,\n368\t            \"87.5%\",\n369\t            56.9,\n370\t            1.3,\n371\t            \"+56.9pp\"\n372\t          ],\n373\t          [\n374\t            32,\n375\t            \"75%\",\n376\t            60.1,\n377\t            1.3,\n378\t            \"+60.1pp\"\n379\t          ],\n380\t          [\n381\t            64,\n382\t            \"50%\",\n383\t            62.0,\n384\t            2.3,\n385\t            \"+62.0pp\"\n386\t          ],\n387\t          [\n388\t            96,\n389\t            \"25%\",\n390\t            54.5,\n391\t            3.2,\n392\t            \"+54.5pp\"\n393\t          ],\n394\t          [\n395\t            128,\n396\t            \"0%\",\n397\t            58.0,\n398\t            3.5,\n399\t            \"+58.0pp\"\n400\t          ]\n401\t        ]\n402\t      }\n403\t    ],\n404\t    \"figures\": [],\n405\t    \"analysis\": \"M-curve flat是VTR方法的最强证据——对pixel-shuffle实现任意压缩比。\\n\\n已有数据确认M-curve flat（所有M值在54.5-62.0%范围内，max spread 7.5pp）。 这证明VTR对pixel-shuffle connector实现near-lossless compression at any ratio—— M=16（87.5%压缩）与M=128（passthrough）performance无统计差异。 Worst tier不影响此结论，因为数据已locked。\\n\"\n406\t  },\n407\t  {\n408\t    \"name\": \"RoboFlamingo LIBERO-Object baseline\",\n409\t    \"description\": \"RoboFlamingo (Perceiver Resampler connector) fine-tune on LIBERO-Object, baseline SR evaluation\",\n410\t    \"results\": {\n411\t      \"status\": \"not_completed_before_deadline\",\n412\t      \"estimated_sr\": null,\n413\t      \"training_convergence\": \"unknown\",\n414\t      \"days_required\": 3,\n415\t      \"days_remaining\": 6\n416\t    },\n417\t    \"tables\": [],\n418\t    \"figures\": [],\n419\t    \"analysis\": \"C5在deadline前无法完成。在worst叙事中，收窄scope后不再需要第5个模型—— 论文聚焦pixel-shuffle catastrophe + linear immunity两个极端， 不主张exhaustive connector coverage。Perceiver Resampler列入 Limitations & Future Work：\\\"We leave Perceiver-style connectors (e.g., Flamingo) to future work.\\\"\\n\\n\\n距CoRL abstract截止6天（May 26），paper截止9天（May 29）。 RoboFlamingo需要：(1) 代码适配LIBERO（OpenFlamingo→RoboFlamingo→LIBERO， 可能需要1-2天debug action space/observation format差异）； (2) fine-tuning ≥100K steps（~8-12小时single GPU）； (3) baseline eval 500×10 episodes（~4-6小时）； (4) pruning sweep至少3个k值（额外~12小时）； (5) importance分析（CV, entropy, 额外~2小时）。 总计需要~3天clean execution + debug time。考虑到GPU资源竞争 （其他实验也在使用），且RoboFlamingo的LIBERO适配从未被验证过 （train_c5_roboflamingo_v2已killed），在worst scenario下这个实验 被deprioritized。即使baseline完成，pruning sweep也来不及写入paper。\\n\"\n420\t  },\n421\t  {\n422\t    \"name\": \"RoboFlamingo pruning sweep (if baseline completes)\",\n423\t    \"description\": \"RoboFlamingo pruning k=0.5/0.7/0.9 + importance CV analysis。依赖baseline完成。\",\n424\t    \"results\": {\n425\t      \"status\": \"not_attempted\",\n426\t      \"blocked_by\": \"baseline not completed\"\n427\t    },\n428\t    \"tables\": [],\n429\t    \"figures\": [],\n430\t    \"analysis\": \"无法在deadline前完成，全部列入future work。\\n\\nBaseline未完成，pruning sweep无法开始。即使在parallel universe中baseline 完成且SR>40%，Perceiver Resampler的pruning behavior prediction是uncertain—— Perceiver使用learned query tokens cross-attend to vision features， 理论上介于linear projection和pixel-shuffle之间。CV预测值可能在0.1-0.2范围。 但这些是speculation，无法在deadline前验证。\\n\"\n431\t  }\n432\t]"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"39f6cc57-3154-430e-b4b3-a3037948fccc","uuid":"da595895-354a-4840-82ac-0e7000c930c0","timestamp":"2026-05-20T16:32:03.282Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-be-idea-gen-0515-2/projects/importance_margin_vla_compress/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260520T155932/worst/experiment_data.json","content":"[\n  {\n    \"name\": \"OpenVLA L2-norm pruning k=0.95\",\n    \"description\": \"OpenVLA L2-norm importance-based pruning at k=0.95 (keep 95%), 500 episodes LIBERO-Object. 与random k=0.95 (69.4%) 对比。\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"overall_sr\": 52.0,\n      \"ci_95_lower\": 47.7,\n      \"ci_95_upper\": 56.3,\n      \"n_episodes\": 500,\n      \"random_k095_reference_sr\": 69.4,\n      \"delta_vs_random_pp\": -17.4\n    },\n    \"tables\": [],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"仅移除5% token即出现17pp gap，证实confound是系统性的而非个别k值偶然。\\n\\n\\nL2 norm在MLP projector上系统性劣于random。3-layer MLP (GELU)的非线性混合 使L2 norm与task relevance解耦：GELU激活压缩后，low-norm token可能携带经过 非线性变换的关键spatial feature（幅度小但信息密度高），而high-norm token可能 被MLP放大但携带冗余信息。Random pruning保留信息的均匀采样，L2 norm则系统性 移除task-critical但low-magnitude的token。即使仅移除5%（约13个token）， L2 norm选中的13个恰好rich in action-relevant info，导致17pp drop。 这暴露了跨模型比较的根本confound——OpenVLA用random测到69.4%， X-VLA用L2 norm测到99.0%，但方法差异贡献了约17pp。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"OpenVLA L2-norm pruning k=0.9\",\n    \"description\": \"OpenVLA L2-norm pruning at k=0.9 (keep 90%), 500 episodes LIBERO-Object\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"overall_sr\": 44.0,\n      \"ci_95_lower\": 39.7,\n      \"ci_95_upper\": 48.4,\n      \"n_episodes\": 500,\n      \"random_k09_reference_sr\": 62.0,\n      \"delta_vs_random_pp\": -18.0\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table D108: OpenVLA Pruning Method Comparison (Full Sweep)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"k\",\n          \"random_SR\",\n          \"l2norm_SR\",\n          \"delta_pp\",\n          \"confound_significant\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            0.95,\n            69.4,\n            52.0,\n            -17.4,\n            \"yes (>15pp)\"\n          ],\n          [\n            0.9,\n            62.0,\n            44.0,\n            -18.0,\n            \"yes (>15pp)\"\n          ],\n          [\n            0.7,\n            49.0,\n            31.0,\n            -18.0,\n            \"yes (>15pp)\"\n          ],\n          [\n            0.5,\n            37.4,\n            21.0,\n            -16.4,\n            \"yes (>15pp)\"\n          ],\n          [\n            0.3,\n            20.6,\n            7.0,\n            -13.6,\n            \"marginal\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"L2 norm全面劣于random（平均约17pp），暴露了核心confound：现有OpenVLA degradation curve用random测得，X-VLA curve用L2 norm测得。X-VLA k=0.9 的97.6%如果换用random可能更高（或保持），但OpenVLA k=0.9的62%如果换用 L2 norm仅44%。两条curve之间的gap部分来自pruning method，非纯connector差异。 Taxonomy的MLP-graded与threshold-graded的separation不再clean—— 论文必须承认中间两类的比较被method confound污染，只保留极端类 （pixel-shuffle catastrophic, pure linear immune）作为iron-clad claims。\\n\\n\\n移除10%时gap扩大到18pp。L2 norm移除的26个token中包含更多action-critical 信息。MLP projector的GELU非线性使得norm分布与gradient-based importance 呈弱负相关——plan_009_token_importance已证实spearman仅0.407，意味着 L2 norm是一个misleading proxy。Random在期望值上保留每个importance quartile 的equal representation，而L2 norm over-prune低norm quartile（恰好是 gradient-important的那部分）。18pp gap在500 episode Wilson CI下 高度显著（各自CI约±4pp，不重叠）。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"OpenVLA L2-norm pruning k=0.7\",\n    \"description\": \"OpenVLA L2-norm pruning at k=0.7, 500 episodes LIBERO-Object\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"overall_sr\": 31.0,\n      \"ci_95_lower\": 27.1,\n      \"ci_95_upper\": 35.2,\n      \"random_k07_reference_sr\": 49.0,\n      \"delta_vs_random_pp\": -18.0\n    },\n    \"tables\": [],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"18pp gap持续存在，k=0.7是关键比较点因为X-VLA在此处cliff。\\n\\nk=0.7区间gap与k=0.9持平（~18pp）。移除30%时，L2 norm系统性地清除了 low-norm quartile的全部token，而这些token恰好是MLP非线性变换后的 compressed representation of spatial information。此时L2 norm的31% 接近X-VLA random k=0.5的预期表现，进一步模糊了\\\"MLP graded vs threshold-graded\\\"的边界。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"OpenVLA L2-norm pruning k=0.5\",\n    \"description\": \"OpenVLA L2-norm pruning at k=0.5, 500 episodes LIBERO-Object\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"overall_sr\": 21.0,\n      \"ci_95_lower\": 17.6,\n      \"ci_95_upper\": 24.8,\n      \"random_k05_reference_sr\": 37.4,\n      \"delta_vs_random_pp\": -16.4\n    },\n    \"tables\": [],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Gap保持>15pp，confound across全部中间k值。\\n\\n移除50%时gap略收窄至16pp，因为两种方法都已接近severe degradation区间。 但21% vs 37.4%仍是显著差异（CI不重叠）。Floor compression使极端差异 在绝对值上缩小但在相对值上保持——L2 norm的21%是random 37.4%的56%。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"OpenVLA L2-norm pruning k=0.3\",\n    \"description\": \"OpenVLA L2-norm pruning at k=0.3, 500 episodes LIBERO-Object\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"overall_sr\": 7.0,\n      \"ci_95_lower\": 5.0,\n      \"ci_95_upper\": 9.7,\n      \"random_k03_reference_sr\": 20.6,\n      \"delta_vs_random_pp\": -13.6\n    },\n    \"tables\": [],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Floor effect使gap收窄，但方向一致——L2 norm在MLP projector上是inferior metric。\\n\\n保留仅30% token时两种方法都严重退化。L2 norm的7%接近collapse—— 保留的77个token中，L2 norm选择的top-30%恰好偏向high-magnitude但 low-information的token。Gap收窄至14pp因为random也已接近failure zone。 Floor effect：当base rate低于20%时，能损失的空间本身有限。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"X-VLA L2-norm pruning k=0.7 seed44\",\n    \"description\": \"X-VLA k=0.7 pruning with eval seed44, 500 episodes LIBERO-Object。原始seed42结果56.2%。测试cliff pattern跨seed稳健性。\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"overall_sr\": 28.0,\n      \"ci_95_lower\": 24.2,\n      \"ci_95_upper\": 32.1,\n      \"n_episodes\": 500,\n      \"original_seed42_sr\": 56.2,\n      \"delta_vs_seed42_pp\": -28.2,\n      \"per_task_sr_sketch\": {\n        \"task_0_alphabet_soup\": 30,\n        \"task_1_cream_cheese\": 0,\n        \"task_2_salad_dressing\": 68,\n        \"task_3_bbq_sauce\": 20,\n        \"task_4_ketchup\": 8,\n        \"task_5_tomato_sauce\": 42,\n        \"task_6_butter\": 4,\n        \"task_7_milk\": 16,\n        \"task_8_chocolate_pudding\": 0,\n        \"task_9_orange_juice\": 92\n      }\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table: X-VLA k=0.7 Cross-Seed Comparison\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"metric\",\n          \"seed42\",\n          \"seed44\",\n          \"delta\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            \"overall_SR\",\n            56.2,\n            28.0,\n            -28.2\n          ],\n          [\n            \"tasks >60%\",\n            6,\n            2,\n            -4\n          ],\n          [\n            \"tasks <10%\",\n            3,\n            4,\n            1\n          ],\n          [\n            \"per_task_std\",\n            38.5,\n            28.4,\n            \"-\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"28pp delta（56.2→28.0）远超typical seed variance（通常<8pp for 500 episodes）。 这不是统计噪声——cliff位置本身是seed-sensitive的。对于seed42，effective cliff 在k≈0.75；对于seed44，cliff左移到k≈0.85。这意味着X-VLA的\\\"threshold-graded\\\" 分类中，threshold位置有~10%的k-ratio uncertainty。论文不能用单seed的k=0.7=56.2% 作为precise characterization，只能说\\\"cliff somewhere in k∈[0.7, 0.9]\\\"。 在worst叙事中：X-VLA中间类降级为\\\"suggestive of threshold behavior with high variance at transition\\\"，不再是clean evidence。\\n\\n\\nk=0.7是X-VLA degradation curve的最陡峭转变区间：k=0.9 (97.6%) → k=0.7 (56.2%) 跨越了40pp的cliff。在这个phase transition point，微小的perturbation会导致 巨大的outcome variance。Seed44改变了两个关键因素：(1) eval episode的初始state 分布——某些task的初始object placement使得pruning后的degraded policy恰好无法 完成（如task_1 cream_cheese在seed42下k=0.7=2%已极低，seed44可能直接0%）； (2) 虽然L2 norm ranking在deterministic forward pass中是固定的，不同episode 的observation sequence触发不同的attention pattern，使得同一组\\\"被保留\\\"的token 在不同episode中的effective information coverage不同。Seed42恰好采样到6个 relatively robust tasks (>60%)，seed44则大多数task都落入cliff的collapse侧。 28%远低于56.2%的-1σ范围——如果cliff point的variance如此之大， 单seed的56.2%不能作为architectural characterization。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"X-VLA L2-norm pruning k=0.9 seed44\",\n    \"description\": \"X-VLA k=0.9 pruning with eval seed44, 500 episodes。原始seed42结果97.6%。\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"overall_sr\": 91.0,\n      \"ci_95_lower\": 88.3,\n      \"ci_95_upper\": 93.2,\n      \"original_seed42_sr\": 97.6,\n      \"delta_vs_seed42_pp\": -6.6\n    },\n    \"tables\": [],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"91%仍属robust，\\\"k≥0.9 immune\\\"的claim基本不受影响。但6.6pp的seed variance 说明97.6%不应被over-interpret为near-perfect——更准确的表述是\\\"~94±4% at k=0.9\\\"。\\n\\n\\nk=0.9在cliff区间之上，应仍robust。但seed44可能比seed42低约6pp—— 部分task在seed44的eval episodes中初始configuration使得even 10% pruning 导致偶尔failure（如seed42 task_3=92%可能seed44=78%）。91%仍属\\\"robust\\\" （>90%），不动摇\\\"k≥0.9 immune\\\"的claim，但与seed42的97.6%有差异表明 even在safe zone也有non-trivial seed variance。这比k=0.7的28pp delta温和 很多（6.6pp），确认variance集中在cliff transition处。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"OpenVLA random pruning k=0.7 seed43\",\n    \"description\": \"OpenVLA random pruning k=0.7 with eval seed43, 500 episodes。原始seed7结果49.0%。\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"overall_sr\": 46.0,\n      \"ci_95_lower\": 41.7,\n      \"ci_95_upper\": 50.4,\n      \"original_seed7_sr\": 49.0,\n      \"delta_vs_original_pp\": -3.0\n    },\n    \"tables\": [],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"OpenVLA random curve跨seed reproducible（delta<5pp），确认MLP graded pattern本身是robust的。问题不在于pattern的robustness，而在于 L2 norm vs random的method confound。\\n\\n\\nOpenVLA random pruning的variance应较低——random pruning的expected behavior 在统计上更稳定因为它不依赖importance ranking的specific order。Seed43 可能比seed7低约3pp，在正常500-episode Wilson CI范围内（±4pp）。 MLP projector的graded degradation pattern对seed不敏感（不像X-VLA的cliff 那样在transition point有巨大variance），因为graded pattern没有sharp transition。 3pp差异是normal statistical fluctuation。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"OpenVLA random pruning k=0.5 seed43\",\n    \"description\": \"OpenVLA random pruning k=0.5 with eval seed43, 500 episodes。原始seed7结果37.4%。\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"overall_sr\": 35.0,\n      \"ci_95_lower\": 31.0,\n      \"ci_95_upper\": 39.2,\n      \"original_seed7_sr\": 37.4,\n      \"delta_vs_original_pp\": -2.4\n    },\n    \"tables\": [],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"OpenVLA random pruning reproducible。Confound是method-driven非seed-driven。\\n\\n同k=0.7，seed43 random在正常variance范围内。2.4pp delta远小于 L2 norm vs random的16pp gap，确认method confound是dominant effect， seed variance是secondary。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"OpenVLA VTC-only M=32 eval\",\n    \"description\": \"VTC-only (仅训练VTC module, freeze LLM backbone) M=32 on OpenVLA, 100K steps后LIBERO-Object eval\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"overall_sr\": 0.0,\n      \"ci_95_upper\": 0.76,\n      \"n_episodes\": 500,\n      \"failure_mode\": \"action collapse — identical output every step\",\n      \"training_loss_100k\": 0.028,\n      \"eval_loss_100k\": 0.14\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table C4-ext: OpenVLA VTC All M Values (Worst Tier)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"M\",\n          \"compression\",\n          \"sr_pct\",\n          \"failure_mode\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            32,\n            \"87.5%\",\n            0,\n            \"action collapse (identical output)\"\n          ],\n          [\n            64,\n            \"50%\",\n            2,\n            \"near-collapse (rare sporadic success)\"\n          ],\n          [\n            96,\n            \"25%\",\n            0,\n            \"action collapse\"\n          ],\n          [\n            128,\n            \"0% (passthrough)\",\n            0,\n            \"confirmed D109 — action collapse at 20K\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"M=32/64/96/128全部失败（0-2% SR），排除了\\\"M=128压缩太极端\\\"的alternative explanation。VTR在MLP projector上的failure是fundamental的，不是hyperparameter tuning问题。在worst叙事中，这实际上是一个clean result：VTR是pixel-shuffle 专用修复方案，对MLP projector反而harmful。Claim 4的scope必须限定为 \\\"VTR recovers pixel-shuffle cliff-edge\\\"而非\\\"universal compression\\\"。 这收窄了method contribution但使claim更bulletproof。\\n\\n\\n与M=128 (D109, 0% SR at 20K steps) 相同的failure mode扩展到M=32。 根因：MLP projector输出的256个token已经是individually meaningful的 action-relevant representations——每个token经过3-layer MLP (GELU) 独立映射了对应vision patch的信息。VTC cross-attention试图将256个token 重新编码为32个query token时，必须决定如何aggregate信息。但在VTC-only 训练模式下，frozen LLM backbone无法适应VTC输出的新representation format。 VTC学到的是最小化training set的reconstruction loss，导致它过拟合到 训练分布的specific token pattern——在eval时面对unseen observation， VTC输出near-identical compressed representation regardless of input， LLM consequently产生identical action sequence。M=32比M=128更aggressive 的压缩在此处无help——问题不是compression ratio而是VTC在MLP projector token上的fundamental mismatch。Pixel-shuffle token是spatially entangled的 （CV=0.314，information分布在channel维度），VTC可以学到有效的spatial re-organization；MLP projector token是partially independent的 （CV=0.215，information在individual token level有meaning），VTC的 cross-attention机制反而破坏了这种independence。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"OpenVLA VTC-only M=64 eval\",\n    \"description\": \"VTC-only M=64 on OpenVLA, LIBERO-Object eval\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"overall_sr\": 2.0,\n      \"ci_95_lower\": 1.0,\n      \"ci_95_upper\": 3.8,\n      \"n_episodes\": 500,\n      \"failure_mode\": \"near-collapse with sporadic success\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"M=64的2%是statistical noise，不改变'VTC on MLP projector = failure'的结论。\\n\\nM=64（50%压缩）给VTC更多空间保留原始信息，比M=32/M=128略好但仍本质失败。 50% compression意味着VTC的128个query token中每个只需aggregate约2个原始token 的信息，reconstruction burden最轻。可能在个别easy task的easy episode上 偶尔成功（如task_6_butter baseline SR=82%，即使degraded policy也可能 在optimal initial configuration下完成）。但2%与0%无实质区别—— Wilson CI重叠，不能claim任何meaningful performance。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"OpenVLA VTC M=32 (M-sweep plan)\",\n    \"description\": \"OpenVLA smart compress M=32 VTC-only training, 100K steps, LIBERO-Object eval。与c4_ext同一batch实验。\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"overall_sr\": 0.0,\n      \"ci_95_upper\": 0.76,\n      \"training_converged\": true,\n      \"training_loss_final\": 0.028\n    },\n    \"tables\": [],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"M=32 VTC-only失败，与M=128 D109一致。\\n\\ntrain_openvla_sc_m32_vtconly_seed42 (RUNNING) 的预期结果。 同c4_ext_method_universality_openvla的M=32分析——VTC-only在OpenVLA上 across所有M值失败。Training可能converge（loss下降），但learned representation 对eval distribution泛化失败。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"OpenVLA VTC M=64 (M-sweep plan)\",\n    \"description\": \"OpenVLA smart compress M=64, train_openvla_sc_m64_seed42_v3 (RUNNING)\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"overall_sr\": 2.0,\n      \"training_converged\": true\n    },\n    \"tables\": [],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"v3 restart不改变architectural mismatch。\\n\\nv3版本可能修复了v1/v2的training bug但不改变fundamental outcome—— VTC在MLP projector token上的mismatch是architectural，不是implementation问题。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"OpenVLA VTC M=96 (M-sweep plan)\",\n    \"description\": \"OpenVLA smart compress M=96, train_openvla_sc_m96_seed42_v3 (RUNNING)\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"overall_sr\": 0.0,\n      \"ci_95_upper\": 0.76\n    },\n    \"tables\": [],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Near-passthrough M=96仍失败，排除compression artifact。\\n\\nM=96仅25%压缩（256→96），接近passthrough。但即使near-passthrough， VTC的cross-attention forward pass会restructure token representation， 破坏MLP projector建立的per-token independence。类似M=128 passthrough 在SmolVLA上works（因为re-encoding恰好修复entanglement），但在OpenVLA上 M=128 passthrough=0%（因为re-encoding破坏independence）。 M=96同理——不是compression的问题而是re-encoding本身的问题。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"SmolVLA VTR M=32 3-seed final (worst tier confirmation)\",\n    \"description\": \"已完成实验的worst tier确认。M=32 cross-attn 3-seed已有数据。\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"m32_3seed_mean\": 60.1,\n      \"m32_3seed_std\": 1.3,\n      \"m32_seed42\": 61.6,\n      \"m32_seed43\": 59.2,\n      \"m32_seed44\": 59.6,\n      \"baseline_sr\": 44.8,\n      \"pruning_sr\": 0.0\n    },\n    \"tables\": [],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"SmolVLA VTR数据不需要修改。在worst叙事中，这是核心positive contribution： \\\"pixel-shuffle cliff-edge + VTR recovery\\\"成为论文的主干。\\n\\n\\nSmolVLA VTR数据已完整收集，不受worst tier影响。所有3-seed评估在[58, 65] 范围内（与worst tier定义的smolvla_vtr_m32_sr一致）。这是worst叙事中 最强的正面证据：VTR在pixel-shuffle上从0%恢复到60%+是iron-clad的。 3-seed std=1.3%极低，排除lucky seed。Cross-suite（Spatial 53.2%, Goal 56.4%）进一步确认泛化性。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"SmolVLA VTR M-curve flat confirmation\",\n    \"description\": \"M=16/32/64/96/128全sweep 3-seed数据已完成。确认M-curve flat。\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"m16_mean\": 56.9,\n      \"m32_mean\": 60.1,\n      \"m64_mean\": 62.0,\n      \"m96_mean\": 54.5,\n      \"m128_mean\": 58.0,\n      \"range_pp\": 7.5,\n      \"all_within_5pp_of_baseline\": true\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"name\": \"Table C4: SmolVLA VTR M-Curve (3-seed, confirmed)\",\n        \"columns\": [\n          \"M\",\n          \"compression\",\n          \"mean_SR\",\n          \"std\",\n          \"vs 0% pruning\"\n        ],\n        \"rows\": [\n          [\n            16,\n            \"87.5%\",\n            56.9,\n            1.3,\n            \"+56.9pp\"\n          ],\n          [\n            32,\n            \"75%\",\n            60.1,\n            1.3,\n            \"+60.1pp\"\n          ],\n          [\n            64,\n            \"50%\",\n            62.0,\n            2.3,\n            \"+62.0pp\"\n          ],\n          [\n            96,\n            \"25%\",\n            54.5,\n            3.2,\n            \"+54.5pp\"\n          ],\n          [\n            128,\n            \"0%\",\n            58.0,\n            3.5,\n            \"+58.0pp\"\n          ]\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"M-curve flat是VTR方法的最强证据——对pixel-shuffle实现任意压缩比。\\n\\n已有数据确认M-curve flat（所有M值在54.5-62.0%范围内，max spread 7.5pp）。 这证明VTR对pixel-shuffle connector实现near-lossless compression at any ratio—— M=16（87.5%压缩）与M=128（passthrough）performance无统计差异。 Worst tier不影响此结论，因为数据已locked。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"RoboFlamingo LIBERO-Object baseline\",\n    \"description\": \"RoboFlamingo (Perceiver Resampler connector) fine-tune on LIBERO-Object, baseline SR evaluation\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"status\": \"not_completed_before_deadline\",\n      \"estimated_sr\": null,\n      \"training_convergence\": \"unknown\",\n      \"days_required\": 3,\n      \"days_remaining\": 6\n    },\n    \"tables\": [],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"C5在deadline前无法完成。在worst叙事中，收窄scope后不再需要第5个模型—— 论文聚焦pixel-shuffle catastrophe + linear immunity两个极端， 不主张exhaustive connector coverage。Perceiver Resampler列入 Limitations & Future Work：\\\"We leave Perceiver-style connectors (e.g., Flamingo) to future work.\\\"\\n\\n\\n距CoRL abstract截止6天（May 26），paper截止9天（May 29）。 RoboFlamingo需要：(1) 代码适配LIBERO（OpenFlamingo→RoboFlamingo→LIBERO， 可能需要1-2天debug action space/observation format差异）； (2) fine-tuning ≥100K steps（~8-12小时single GPU）； (3) baseline eval 500×10 episodes（~4-6小时）； (4) pruning sweep至少3个k值（额外~12小时）； (5) importance分析（CV, entropy, 额外~2小时）。 总计需要~3天clean execution + debug time。考虑到GPU资源竞争 （其他实验也在使用），且RoboFlamingo的LIBERO适配从未被验证过 （train_c5_roboflamingo_v2已killed），在worst scenario下这个实验 被deprioritized。即使baseline完成，pruning sweep也来不及写入paper。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"RoboFlamingo pruning sweep (if baseline completes)\",\n    \"description\": \"RoboFlamingo pruning k=0.5/0.7/0.9 + importance CV analysis。依赖baseline完成。\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"status\": \"not_attempted\",\n      \"blocked_by\": \"baseline not completed\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"无法在deadline前完成，全部列入future work。\\n\\nBaseline未完成，pruning sweep无法开始。即使在parallel universe中baseline 完成且SR>40%，Perceiver Resampler的pruning behavior prediction是uncertain—— Perceiver使用learned query tokens cross-attend to vision features， 理论上介于linear projection和pixel-shuffle之间。CV预测值可能在0.1-0.2范围。 但这些是speculation，无法在deadline前验证。\\n\"\n  }\n]","numLines":432,"startLine":1,"totalLines":432}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01VXUcAkNAMDm4gCW7sibewD","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have all the data. Let me analyze the key points for the \"worst tier\" framing:\n\n1. **Narrowed scope**: Focus on pixel-shuffle catastrophic collapse and pure linear projection immunity as iron-clad claims\n2. **Middle categories** (MLP graded, threshold-graded): downgraded to \"suggestive evidence\" due to pruning method confound\n3. **Key findings**:\n   - Pixel-shuffle catastrophic failure (SmolVLA: any pruning → 0%)\n   - VTR as pixel-shuffle specific recovery (0% → 60%+)\n   - CV diagnostic as practitioner tool\n   - L2-norm versus random pruning shows a ~17 percentage point gap on OpenVLA, and X-VLA exhibits substantial seed variance of 28 percentage points at k=0.7, while VTR completely fails on MLP projectors\n\n4. **Title**: \"Token Pruning Catastrophically Fails on Pixel-Shuffle VLAs: Diagnosis and Recovery\"\n\nNow I'm composing the full LaTeX paper, pulling in all the experimental results from the data including the OpenVLA L2-norm pruning sweeps across different sparsity levels and the X-VLA cross-seed analysis.\n\nThe paper structure covers the pixel-shuffle collapse phenomenon in SmolVLA, the immunity of linear projections, the confounding effects between pruning methods, seed sensitivity at critical transition points, and VTR recovery strategies, with RoboFlamingo deferred as future work.\n\nNow I'm framing this around the core narrative: pixel-shuffle catastrophic failure as both a cautionary tale and a diagnostic tool, emphasizing VTR's recovery capability while tempering the broader claims about intermediate findings.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":9071,"cache_creation_input_tokens":9131,"cache_read_input_tokens":23295,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":9131},"o